{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod","id":932215,"title":"Is it accurate to claim that Werewolves are the best melee fighters in cWoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-15T14:37:51-07:00","id":932215,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Is it accurate to claim that Werewolves are the best melee fighters in cWoD?","content":"I am relatively new to cWoD, and thus far I've seen several claims that a Werewolf can beat all the other monsters in the cWoD in melee combat. Is this accurate? From what I've read in W20 I've seen that an Ahroun in its Crinos form can rip through a LOT of things with ease, but does this also go for the various other monsters?<br /> <br /> I've also seen claims that, when given enough prep time and the right spheres, a Mage can one-shot pretty much anything. But the key points her e are the prep time and the right spheres, so unless the Mage in question is specifically geared towards melee combat they tend to be amongst the weaker of the various monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T15:32:24-07:00","id":932232,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are the best melee fighters <i>on average</i>. It's a key point that's easy to overlook. Werewolves get a lot of innate and easily accessible combat stuff, which means even minimally combat oriented Garou are nasty in a fight, while most supernaturals require dedicated effort to invest in being that good at killing stuff. However, a heavily combat focused member of many of the supernatural types can easily overwhelm a non-combat oriented werewolf, and stay competitive with combat oriented ones (though there's a difficulty here as Renown and Rank are highly variable/subjective and gate higher powers much more than most supernaturals have to deal with).<br /> <br /> Mages need prep, though people often think that means, &quot;lots of extended ritual magic ahead of time,&quot; which isn't always the case. There's a lot mages can do in terms of more basic things - like forming a cabal that shares a mutual focus so they can teamwork cast - that get overlooked. Even with prep though, mages aren't great at melee. They're best at a distance rather than up close and personal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T15:44:37-07:00","id":932235,"title":"","content":"Just posting to note I agree with everything Heavy Arms said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T16:55:53-07:00","id":932252,"title":"","content":"In one on one, with no to little prep, generally its true. However with prep many of the other supers should be able to defeat a garou.. Presence could easily cow them, so could dominate. Obfuscate 4 can make it impossible for them to find you..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:22:19-07:00","id":932262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932252#post932252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one on one, with no to little prep, generally its true. However with prep many of the other supers should be able to defeat a garou.. Presence could easily cow them, so could dominate. Obfuscate 4 can make it impossible for them to find you..</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all big maybes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T20:09:07-07:00","id":932349,"title":"","content":"I'm not too familiar with other Changing Breeds but my understanding is that the tiger ones and the bear ones and possibly the shark ones (werebear holding a wereshark, anyone?) are tougher than werewolves.<br /> <br /> Of course none of these creatures can soak Lethal in breed form, so a bullet to the back of the head of an unsuspecting werecreature can be pretty effective, especially if they're Homid and therefore have the terrible senses and awareness of a human when they're in breed form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T21:46:47-07:00","id":932389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932349#post932349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too familiar with other Changing Breeds but my understanding is that the tiger ones and the bear ones and possibly the shark ones (werebear holding a wereshark, anyone?) are tougher than werewolves.<br /> <br /> Of course none of these creatures can soak Lethal in breed form, so a bullet to the back of the head of an unsuspecting werecreature can be pretty effective, especially if they're Homid and therefore have the terrible senses and awareness of a human when they're in breed form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When we start playing that game a Vampire in day sleep is pretty damn easy to take out, even Gangrel you can always pave over their spot.<br /> <br /> Mage Sphere allow someone to be a very Good Sniper.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the real answer to this is Wererats. Mostly because Dex is the super stat in Melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T22:04:38-07:00","id":932403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932389#post932389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage Sphere allow someone to be a very Good Sniper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially if they have Correspondence. If they know where you are, they can snipe you from across the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932389#post932389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the real answer to this is Wererats. Mostly because Dex is the super stat in Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. Also it seems like they could be numerous, which is a scary thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T00:14:27-07:00","id":932427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932349#post932349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too familiar with other Changing Breeds but my understanding is that the tiger ones and the bear ones and possibly the shark ones (werebear holding a wereshark, anyone?) are tougher than werewolves.<br /> <br /> Of course none of these creatures can soak Lethal in breed form, so a bullet to the back of the head of an unsuspecting werecreature can be pretty effective, especially if they're Homid and therefore have the terrible senses and awareness of a human when they're in breed form.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Mods they get, sure.. A gurahl (Werebear) gets +5 to both Str and Stam in crinos, where Garou get +4/+3.. However the garou get +2 dex iirc, while bears iirc get nothing or just +1..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932403#post932403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932389#post932389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the real answer to this is Wererats. Mostly because Dex is the super stat in Melee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. Also it seems like they could be numerous, which is a scary thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Especially with each success over the to hit you needed adding +1 to damage..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T07:40:15-07:00","id":932500,"title":"","content":"This all generally comes back to the hypothetical white room where everyone punches each other Mortal Kombat style until someone dies. In that scenario, with most other factors being equal (PC tier, amount of XP, combat build, etc.) werewolves are going to win most of the time. The key is to make sure that most factors aren't equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:11:58-07:00","id":932608,"title":"","content":"Exactly.. &quot;He who enters a combat without doing as much as they can to stack the deck in their favor is a fool&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T17:30:21-07:00","id":932692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932349#post932349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not too familiar with other Changing Breeds but my understanding is that the tiger ones and the bear ones and possibly the shark ones (werebear holding a wereshark, anyone?) are tougher than werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Without modifications, generally only the Gurahl have that advantage. With Archid traits, Mokole can be in a league that should rightly not have mechanical expression in standard system terms (being Godzilla-sized means that most things really shouldn't be able to stand up to you), and some Rokea are packing the Gift Leviathan, which allows them to add five to all their huge shark physical Attributes. Finally, Garou and Mokole can both learn a Gift that increases their physical Attributes by their permanent Honor rating, which is only a Rank 2 power; you have to be defending allies or territory that would otherwise be unable to see to that independently in order to use it, though..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course none of these creatures can soak Lethal in breed form, so a bullet to the back of the head of an unsuspecting werecreature can be pretty effective, especially if they're Homid and therefore have the terrible senses and awareness of a human when they're in breed form. </div> </div> </div>Primal-Urge is actually useable in any form, as is Alertness. There's also the possibility of partial shapechanging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:01:14-07:00","id":932730,"title":"","content":"A Dark Ages Fae will pretty much win any white room fight, simply because of unleashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T22:59:34-07:00","id":932802,"title":"","content":"The Devil's Due rules can be used to manufacture high-Torment demons who I think can easily take anything else in the setting (short of a mage cheesing rituals) in a straight brawl with their starting stats thanks to how frontloaded and open-ended the arcana system is. Torment 10 with WP 10 and maximum Taints; 150 form points at char creation means you can take 30 dice of soak (which you can double to 60 dice for a point of Resolve) at difficulty 4. Slap on Gaping Maw, Poison, Speed of Thought, enough trait aptitudes for brawl and perhaps also strength to lower your difficulties to 2, and as many levels of Inhuman Strength and Trait Bonus (strength) as you can manage. Near-invulnerability coupled with quite large aggravated damage dice pools and a repeatable Resolve-scaling celerity effect should be more than enough to win against anything short of a comparably enormous soak pool, and that's without xp expenditure (which will only go to Resolve and conventional attributes, but you can raise the latter as high as your Resolve anyway).<br /> <br /> I think you could min/maxing it get to be something like 6 + 3 (all rolling on 3) + 4 automatic successes aggravated + 5 lethal damage attacks, with a dice pool of 9 to hit (rolling on 2), 30 dice of universal soak rolling on 4 that can be doubled to 60 dice for a turn, with 1-5 extra attacks per turn for up to 5 turns (or 1-6 for 6 if you put a point into Resolve, assuming no Resolve expenditure on soak doubling). This is a character with 0 xp using the starting Resolve rules for a monstrous demon (admittedly in the category of a 'too evil to be playable' by the terms of the rulebook, but within the same mechanical boundaries that the recommended PC setup could attain anyway; the recommended PC taken to the formally appropriate extreme- i.e. Torment 9- would be at Resolve 4 and be down two levels of automatic strength success). An xp-maxed character would have 1-10 extra actions for up to 10 turns as well as 10s in all desired attributes and abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 07-17-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T09:36:51-07:00","id":932935,"title":"","content":"Once you get to min-maxing weirdness, it kind of invalidates the &quot;typical member of the type&quot; arguments. I can write up a starter Fomori that can kill almost anything using their rules. that doesn't make Fomori in general any more powerful.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms response above more or less explains my point of view as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T10:54:22-07:00","id":932966,"title":"","content":"On general, shapeshifters rule combat, though Kitsune should always run alway because they lack regen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:50:02-07:00","id":932984,"title":"","content":"The Fera (again on average different ones have different strengths and weaknesses) rule <i>white room</i> combat.<br /> <br /> The more you making the combat a &quot;real world&quot; set up, the more the other supernaturals can stand up to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T12:20:24-07:00","id":932993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932966#post932966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On general, shapeshifters rule combat, though Kitsune should always run alway because they lack regen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Unless they have it as a Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:50:20-07:00","id":933033,"title":"","content":"I am just talking about beginning characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T13:54:57-07:00","id":933038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=932935#post932935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you get to min-maxing weirdness, it kind of invalidates the &quot;typical member of the type&quot; arguments. I can write up a starter Fomori that can kill almost anything using their rules. that doesn't make Fomori in general any more powerful.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms response above more or less explains my point of view as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.. ANyone using most any system, can create up a munchkin o doom that would generally wipe the floor with any other super out there..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T20:45:09-07:00","id":933232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933033#post933033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am just talking about beginning characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I hate bildungsroman stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T20:59:44-07:00","id":933236,"title":"","content":"I do not know if it is possible to make a beginning combat maximized fomori that could stand toe-to-toe with a beginning combat maximized Garou. If the Autonomy of a fomori drops below the Willpower of its associated spirit, it is basically the spirit's toy and does what the spirit wants. That means that fomori averages around 25 Power Points before it becomes useless and buggers off to do the spirit's bidding. I know, however, that no beginning combat optimized vampire can go toe-to-toe with a beginning combat optimized werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T21:28:19-07:00","id":933250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933236#post933236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know if it is possible to make a beginning combat maximized fomori that could stand toe-to-toe with a beginning combat maximized Garou. If the Autonomy of a fomori drops below the Willpower of its associated spirit, it is basically the spirit's toy and does what the spirit wants. That means that fomori averages around 25 Power Points before it becomes useless and buggers off to do the spirit's bidding. I know, however, that no beginning combat optimized vampire can go toe-to-toe with a beginning combat optimized werewolf</div> </div> </div> </div>Just balance powers with taints instead of with autonomy. and Homogenity works wonders as an equalizer power (against most supernaturals). then just tack on Take the True Form and some absurd combat abilities. You have a fomori that can force creatures to stay in human form and cancel out any supernatural abilities. They are short lived due to the amount of taints you are forced to take, but they are very effective. It just in no way represents what &quot;normal&quot; fomori are like.<br /> You can build Bygone Beasts similarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T21:36:09-07:00","id":933254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933033#post933033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am just talking about beginning characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not most of the people here.<br /> <br /> Really WOD combat heavily values alpha strikes. Dexterity is better than any other physical stat in combat. Extra actions are insanely powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T03:30:23-07:00","id":933340,"title":"","content":"In most cases, the additional actions per turn are the means for combat prowess. Garou have them integrated, which is their huge bonus compared to Gurahl, or most other beings. Starting Devil's due demons not withstanding.<br /> Then again, a changeling start character with Quicksilver as Art and Time as Realm can for a specific point in the future accumulate and unlimited number of successes, which translates into addition actions.<br /> <br /> Then a Mokol\u00e9 with only &quot;huge size&quot;, might be able to simplay body slam everything he sees. Even if that doesn't kill (or even damage) a 30 soak dice demon, the Mokol\u00e9 can just sit on him...<br /> <br /> Also, Puppetry is quite nice in a fight with someone living. Since a wraith is mostly unharmed by living beings anyway...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T12:46:33-07:00","id":933536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933340#post933340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most cases, the additional actions per turn are the means for combat prowess. Garou have them integrated, which is their huge bonus compared to Gurahl, or most other beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bearfolk DO get shafted in that regard, being they are the only shifters i know of who CAN'T gain extra actions via rage (or through spending blood like Anaassi).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933340#post933340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then a Mokol\u00e9 with only &quot;huge size&quot;, might be able to simplay body slam everything he sees. Even if that doesn't kill (or even damage) a 30 soak dice demon, the Mokol\u00e9 can just sit on him...<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of hard to attack, when you are being squished by a 2000+lb gator!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T17:33:53-07:00","id":933661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933536#post933536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of hard to attack, when you are being squished by a 2000+lb gator!</div> </div> </div> </div>One short ton is the rather extreme small end of how big a Mokole can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T18:03:36-07:00","id":933667,"title":"","content":"If we're talking about demons though, don't most have fairly nasty mystical abilities that wouldn't be hampered by being pinned under something the way a mage's spells might?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T19:40:47-07:00","id":933706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933667#post933667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about demons though, don't most have fairly nasty mystical abilities that wouldn't be hampered by being pinned under something the way a mage's spells might?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pinned under quickly becomes crushed into a pancake. Especially with a Mokole 256 (2^8, say five purchases of Tall and three of Behemoth, not that they ever should have really been split up) times larger than usual. Which is, itself, a rather large lowball; I'd place both those Traits as tripling weight per purchase, or nearly so, due to auxiliary dimensional size increases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T22:58:54-07:00","id":933742,"title":"","content":"Wow, mokole sound insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T23:06:01-07:00","id":933751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933667#post933667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about demons though, don't most have fairly nasty mystical abilities that wouldn't be hampered by being pinned under something the way a mage's spells might?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Do they need to breath to activate those magical powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:06:33-07:00","id":933853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933742#post933742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, mokole sound insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mokole are insane, which is why they are fun, though they are vulnerable to gold and silver. While weapons of gold and silver are rare, they are common in jewelry, and I would rule that someone sporting a gold ring (or silver ring) on each finger could punch for aggravated and unsoakable damage against a Mokole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:14:07-07:00","id":933857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933853#post933853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mokole are insane, which is why they are fun, though they are vulnerable to gold and silver. While weapons of gold and silver are rare, they are common in jewelry, and I would rule that someone sporting a gold ring (or silver ring) on each finger could punch for aggravated and unsoakable damage against a Mokole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that the books state somewhere that that isn't how it works. Said punch, it if the persons fingers were absolutely covered is jewelry would do punch damage (soaked as normal) +1 level of Agg (unsoakable).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:28:43-07:00","id":933864,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:51:51-07:00","id":934028,"title":"","content":"Very true, mokole are combat monsters if built right (and the ST doesn't reign it in), however they pay for that with 2 bane metals, ONLY 3 forms they can shift into/from (unlike most all the rest with 5), and also only start with 2 gifts, vice 3!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T13:33:27-07:00","id":934055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934028#post934028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Very true, mokole are combat monsters if built right (and the ST doesn't reign it in), however they pay for that with 2 bane metals, ONLY 3 forms they can shift into/from (unlike most all the rest with 5), and also only start with 2 gifts, vice 3!</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've never viewed the Changers with 3 forms as being at a disadvantage. They shift easier between forms at the ends of the spectrum which is a plus. Along with that, they rarely (if ever) only make it partway and end up in an awkward form.<br /> Mokole (and Rokea as well) really do get screwed though, getting only 2 Gifts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T16:25:11-07:00","id":934162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934028#post934028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true, mokole are combat monsters if built right (and the ST doesn't reign it in), however they pay for that with 2 bane metals, ONLY 3 forms they can shift into/from (unlike most all the rest with 5), and also only start with 2 gifts, vice 3!</div> </div> </div> </div>They get a near-human form as a second rank Gift. Enter the Reptoid!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T16:51:43-07:00","id":934178,"title":"","content":"Rokea have five forms in revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T17:06:28-07:00","id":934188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934178#post934178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rokea have five forms in revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>4 and half...sort of. It's weird. Only the Betweeners developed the Glabro equivalent form, and even then, its dif 8 or 9 to get into.<br /> &quot;Normal&quot; Rokea go straight from Gladius (Crinos) to homid with no in between.<br /> I know the writers were trying to do something interesting with it, but that ends up raising more questions than it answers. Mokole have a dreamed form, so they're different altogether. I wonder if the Corax just haven't practiced enough to find Glabro and Hispo equivalent forms. Go go giant war raven! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T18:34:43-07:00","id":934228,"title":"","content":"These kinds of discussions come up all the time. I want to point out that if you are playing the game to build the most bad ass melee fighter, then you have missed the point. Even ahroun (the warriors for the race that has Rage as a major aspect of their very soul) do not live to only fight. They have other goals.<br /> <br /> These white room scenarios rarely yield anything more than people talking about their favorite race and how they can make that race be the nastiest ever. And at some point, you get someone mentioning how Mage always wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:08:00-07:00","id":934271,"title":"","content":"True, but it is a way to figure out game balance and, more importantly, for an ST to understand what breaks in a system. For example, Garou are capable of defeating most other changing breeds because of a mixture of pack tactics and klaives. If you want to cause your Garou to brown their shorts, so to speak, have them face a combat optimized beginning Gurahl with the Silver Tolerance Merit. A normal pack of five Garou will be running for the hills when they start to understand that it is soaking their Klaives damage without blinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:41:44-07:00","id":934281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934271#post934271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but it is a way to figure out game balance and, more importantly, for an ST to understand what breaks in a system. For example, Garou are capable of defeating most other changing breeds because of a mixture of pack tactics and klaives. If you want to cause your Garou to brown their shorts, so to speak, have them face a combat optimized beginning Gurahl with the Silver Tolerance Merit. A normal pack of five Garou will be running for the hills when they start to understand that it is soaking their Klaives damage without blinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this premise, if not the conclusion. Knowing what breaks the system allows you to fix it and run things differently for your games. Using cheats (my words, not yours) to exploit the system to present challenges to the players goes against the spirit of a storytelling game imo. Also, I think maybe (I don't know) you are under the impression that there are a lot more klaives being wielded by Garou packs than there actually are. In most games I've played, the players aren't running around with an abundance of silver. A pack of Garou is going to tear through a &quot;beginning Gurahl&quot; (no matter how combat optimized) with very little effort if they have any sort of teamwork at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934228#post934228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These kinds of discussions come up all the time. I want to point out that if you are playing the game to build the most bad ass melee fighter, then you have missed the point. Even ahroun (the warriors for the race that has Rage as a major aspect of their very soul) do not live to only fight. They have other goals.<br /> <br /> These white room scenarios rarely yield anything more than people talking about their favorite race and how they can make that race be the nastiest ever. And at some point, you get someone mentioning how Mage always wins.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, while the initial idea of the thread normally amounts to comparing white room scenario combats, several interesting ideas have been brought up that are worth thinking about from a balance perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:45:32-07:00","id":934286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934055#post934055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I've never viewed the Changers with 3 forms as being at a disadvantage. They shift easier between forms at the ends of the spectrum which is a plus. Along with that, they rarely (if ever) only make it partway and end up in an awkward form.<br /> Mokole (and Rokea as well) really do get screwed though, getting only 2 Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but shifting to say Glabro for garou or hispo (for lupus breed garou) was always a benefit for them.. Gave them some boosts, without going hole hock into delerium causing crinos..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934162#post934162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They get a near-human form as a second rank Gift. Enter the Reptoid!</div> </div> </div> </div>But you have to pop one of their gifts to do that..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T21:57:14-07:00","id":934291,"title":"","content":"The Fair Glabro Merit is worth getting for the majority of shapeshifters. It allows them to use a 'super' form that soaks any type of damage and regenerates without alienating humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T01:15:43-07:00","id":934345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=933667#post933667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about demons though, don't most have fairly nasty mystical abilities that wouldn't be hampered by being pinned under something the way a mage's spells might?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death 4: Extinguish Life. Strength + Awareness: beat the target's Stamina and it dies. High-Torment does this to all within #Faith in yards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T06:55:15-07:00","id":934462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934345#post934345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death 4: Extinguish Life. Strength + Awareness: beat the target's Stamina and it dies. High-Torment does this to all within #Faith in yards.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the ridiculous example of a Mokole given above, there is no realistic chance of beating its Stamina (which will be somewhere in the teens).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:17:48-07:00","id":934643,"title":"","content":"Stamina 19, if I remember correctly, when in Archid form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:00:43-07:00","id":934669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934291#post934291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fair Glabro Merit is worth getting for the majority of shapeshifters. It allows them to use a 'super' form that soaks any type of damage and regenerates without alienating humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its actually rare for me as a ST to see players of Werewolf to take that merit.. Most just jack up the appearance and stay in glabro anyway, so the loss is not as meaningful..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:01:35-07:00","id":934670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934462#post934462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the ridiculous example of a Mokole given above, there is no realistic chance of beating its Stamina (which will be somewhere in the teens).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to start a thread on having some actually post their characters ,made up AS per proper rules (no munchkinning out), just to see how things go..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:26:53-07:00","id":934707,"title":"","content":"The ten levels of Huge Size are actually used in an Apocalypse scenario for the Mokole, if I remember correctly, as they have around a dozen elder Mokole sleeping eternally to be woken up during the end days with that build, one the assumption that they would be almost unstoppable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:01:52-07:00","id":934786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934707#post934707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ten levels of Huge Size are actually used in an Apocalypse scenario for the Mokole, if I remember correctly, as they have around a dozen elder Mokole sleeping eternally to be woken up during the end days with that build, one the assumption that they would be almost unstoppable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mostly for the Weaver Ascendant scenario, which put giant Archid rampages on the table of suggested ways to deal with the skyrocketing Gauntlet. Take down a city, and the barrier weakens; as it so happens, Mokole can accomplish this largely just by walking around in such a form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:46:45-07:00","id":934819,"title":"","content":"Though I would suggest that a Mokole with that build needs Silver Tolerance and Gold Tolerance Merits to be truly effective, as it will be nearly impossible for their enemies to miss them in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:42:42-07:00","id":934920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934819#post934819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I would suggest that a Mokole with that build needs Silver Tolerance and Gold Tolerance Merits to be truly effective, as it will be nearly impossible for their enemies to miss them in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be that the rules haven't caught up to the concerns of their size and that you'd need a (puts on sunglasses) properly-scaled weapon to actually deal damage to them. So, in order to deal knife damage to a Godzilla-sized Archid form, you'd need something that was good-quality gold or sterling-purity silver and also would be the size of a small building. See the demolition rules in Hunter Book: Avenger for examples of the size scale, and consider how absurdly expensive it would be. Not impossible, of course, but hideously, hideously expensive, and likely only good for one hit as it collapses under its own weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T00:00:42-07:00","id":934939,"title":"","content":"Mokole are alot less impressive than they should be in theory. First in their combat form they are -1 Dex. While when they can hit they can do a lot of damage.. not being hit is an advantage many Fera have over it with a Dex bonus. Second Mokole don't have any gifts that allow them to increase their iniative like say spirit of the Fray. Finally for all the size bonus they don't get anything like a strength bonus, they get stamina and that can readily be undercut by bringing Silver/gold.<br /> <br /> Godzilla is really more of a trap build for the Mokole","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T00:22:09-07:00","id":934941,"title":"","content":"I've never understood that whole -1dex in archid for them. Having seen plenty of documentaries on reptiles, they are OFTEN very dexterous.. So that mod SHOULD have imo been +1...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T04:53:15-07:00","id":934996,"title":"","content":"The worst (as in, nightmare fuel) thing that I can think of in the WoD, when it comes to a pure 'Punch/claw-the-enemy-til-it-dies' type of combat, is an Ananasi of the Wyrsta faction at Rank 3+.<br /> <br /> Hint: Blood Pump + Tick Body. Add Hydraulic Strength in case of Rank 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-21-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T07:43:26-07:00","id":935056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=934939#post934939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mokole are alot less impressive than they should be in theory. First in their combat form they are -1 Dex. While when they can hit they can do a lot of damage.. not being hit is an advantage many Fera have over it with a Dex bonus. Second Mokole don't have any gifts that allow them to increase their iniative like say spirit of the Fray. Finally for all the size bonus they don't get anything like a strength bonus, they get stamina and that can readily be undercut by bringing Silver/gold.<br /> <br /> Godzilla is really more of a trap build for the Mokole</div> </div> </div> </div>It confounds me why the pieces of Huge Size do what they do instead of cutting down on how big Mokole can be in Archid and making Dream Semblance grant a form that's huge, in addition to its one per lifetime effect. Then we could all be talking about obscene numbers of purchases for Armor instead! 30+ dice to soak, once Gifts come into play! (^VVVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> (Terrible Claws and Long Teeth also being a shit show, since they add... one die of damage. Persistently, but you can only get them once, and they don't do anything else. So not worth it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:17:43-07:00","id":935152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935056#post935056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It confounds me why the pieces of Huge Size do what they do instead of cutting down on how big Mokole can be in Archid and making Dream Semblance grant a form that's huge, in addition to its one per lifetime effect. Then we could all be talking about obscene numbers of purchases for Armor instead! 30+ dice to soak, once Gifts come into play! (^VVVVVVV^)</div> </div> </div> </div>Soak is still a poor man's game.<br /> <br /> But what I'm trying to point out with Kaiju build is its not mechanically supported to do what it looks like it should. I mean &quot;City Destroyer&quot; seems like its dooable ... but they don't get a strength Bonus or a bonus to destroying things or what have you, a Gurhal can more readily pull the &quot;great city destroyer&quot; combo with its rage and build than the so called &quot;Godzilla&quot; types.<br /> <br /> People point out it should require a lot of Gold to Hurt the Kaiju build but they don't even get bonus health levels they get Stamina....which is readily bypassed. Its not mechanically supported whatsoever for whatever claims of it being a Munchkin build.<br /> <br /> This is before the fact you basically can't do shit with it because of the Veil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Terrible Claws and Long Teeth also being a shit show, since they add... one die of damage. Persistently, but you can only get them once, and they don't do anything else. So not worth it.) </div> </div> </div>Grasping hands is where its at, one reading of it says it removes the Dex penalty, and even if it doesn't the ability to properly use weapons Fetishes beats claws and Teeth. Prehensile tail and upright walking..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:20:10-07:00","id":935189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935152#post935152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean &quot;City Destroyer&quot; seems like its dooable ... but they don't get a strength Bonus or a bonus to destroying things or what have you</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I personally think, final strength should be calculated in some WoD games as strength * sizefactor. Whatever the scale definition of that factor would be.<br /> <br /> Likewise, dodging should be *improved* by a smaller size. athletics / sizefactor?<br /> Werewolf has some elements of size changeing, and Mage especially does have several ways of changeing size (Not all of them technically changing strength logically though).<br /> Not sure about the other games, but I bet Demon and Changeling do as well.<br /> <br /> It might overcomplicate things a leeeettle bit, but it might make for an optional houserule if so desired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:15:57-07:00","id":935257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935189#post935189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I personally think, final strength should be calculated in some WoD games as strength * sizefactor. Whatever the scale definition of that factor would be.<br /> <br /> Likewise, dodging should be *improved* by a smaller size. athletics / sizefactor?<br /> Werewolf has some elements of size changeing, and Mage especially does have several ways of changeing size (Not all of them technically changing strength logically though).<br /> Not sure about the other games, but I bet Demon and Changeling do as well.<br /> <br /> It might overcomplicate things a leeeettle bit, but it might make for an optional houserule if so desired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of like how WEG Star wars had scaling systems. Bigger target were EASIER to hit by smaller ones, but did often less damage, while bigger targets had a harder time hitting smaller ones, but if hit, did more damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T19:43:51-07:00","id":935426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod#post932215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am relatively new to cWoD, and thus far I've seen several claims that a Werewolf can beat all the other monsters in the cWoD in melee combat. Is this accurate? From what I've read in W20 I've seen that an Ahroun in its Crinos form can rip through a LOT of things with ease, but does this also go for the various other monsters?<br /> <br /> I've also seen claims that, when given enough prep time and the right spheres, a Mage can one-shot pretty much anything. But the key points her e are the prep time and the right spheres, so unless the Mage in question is specifically geared towards melee combat they tend to be amongst the weaker of the various monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As they told you it depends on the context.<br /> <br /> On average a Werewolf is way stronger than a vampire when it comes to melee fight.<br /> <br /> Still context is vital.<br /> Just few werewolves would be able to survive a strong elder like Jalav-Ajan (nevertheless even here circumstances play a big role, a toreador elder is going to have MUCH less chances to survive than a Gangrel elder) and a mage who could pull the Shivasakti Ayvatara effect would be a deadly foe for anyone.<br /> <br /> Vampires and mages tend to get more powerfull than werewolf with time: Vampires can get their stats and disciplines higher than most other creatures and mages can do almost everything as their mastery grows.<br /> Still, the most powerfull Vampires and Mages are usually NPC: while it's not impossibile for a Werewolf player to get Rank 5 it's doesn't happen often that a Mage player ascends to the rank of Archmage, and it's mostly impossible for a Vampire player to become a methuselah, unless you're playing a munchkin campaign.<br /> <br /> So if we are speaking about average starting playable character then yes, a werewolf is really tough stuff*, but then if we are taking in account also NPC then no, no werewolf will beat by brute force Enkidu or Voormas.<br /> In those cases well devised plans and pack tactics should be the main focus.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for mages the same rule can be applied here: context is everything.<br /> A master mage can do almost anything, still paradox can be a bitch: beeing able to do something in theory is not the same as actually doing it.<br /> Paradox is the real obstacle: with time magic (contingency effect with time 3) and rituals a mage can prepare himself without trouble,<br /> Even so there are high chances that paradox will bite him in the ass: one shot kill spells are usually pretty vulgar effect, Mr Wrinkle and Judgment may have their say about you using them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *But even here we should look at circumstances: while a Arhoun Get of Fenris player should be a dreadful foe for most vampires in melee fight (he could easily split open the average gangrel joe, without much effort), would that be true even when direct fight is not on the table? For instance, if a Get of Fenris without Shell gift cross is path with a Ventrue or a Tremere (both really good at domination) what would happen?<br /> Most likely it would start dancing as a monkey for his new master.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-21-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T20:52:25-07:00","id":935439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935426#post935426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As they told you it depends on the context.<br /> <br /> On average a Werewolf is way stronger than a vampire when it comes to melee fight.<br /> <br /> Still context is vital.<br /> Just few werewolves would be able to survive a strong elder like Jalav-Ajan (nevertheless even here circumstances play a big role, a toreador elder is going to have MUCH less chances to survive than a Gangrel elder) and a mage who could pull the Shivasakti Ayvatara effect would be a deadly foe for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity, Auspex and Presence is pretty much a super survival option. It may not kick the shit out of werewolves but knows they are coming, can run really fast and makes them not want to hit you..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T21:02:39-07:00","id":935440,"title":"","content":"The best options for everyone is just to avoid combat with werewolves. Unless you are working with Pentex or one of the other groups associated with the Wyrm, you can easily avoid combat with werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T23:00:08-07:00","id":935458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935440#post935440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best options for everyone is just to avoid combat with werewolves. Unless you are working with Pentex or one of the other groups associated with the Wyrm, you can easily avoid combat with werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Don't get into direct combat. Use alter means.. Dominate some humans to attack with flame throwers and such. Presence on the town hall magistrates and declare their 'homes' derelict property to be bulldozed over for a new shopping complex.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T00:01:10-07:00","id":935469,"title":"","content":"How powerful are mumies in combat? I know they're not Arisen powerful but have some high power rituals. So how powerful are they in a straight up fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:13:28-07:00","id":935489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935439#post935439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celerity, Auspex and Presence is pretty much a super survival option. It may not kick the shit out of werewolves but knows they are coming, can run really fast and makes them not want to hit you..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed.<br /> <br /> While young Vampires are at real disadvantage in melee fight with garou they also have all the necessary means to avoid fighting them.<br /> Besides the rule I mentioned before for the Garou vs Methuselah/Archmage applies for young vampires also : group tactic, clever plans and a bit of cunning can always do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-22-2016, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:24:17-07:00","id":935491,"title":"","content":"Also, something that musn't be ignored with V20/DAV20:<br /> Celerity, Potence and Fortitude (when not activated with blood) passively give you extra dice to anything Dex, Strength and Stamina *on top* of any normal stats you boosted with bloodpoints.<br /> <br /> It is technically possible to make a constant-10-dex (or strength, or stamina..) non-elder Vampire straight out of chargen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-22-2016, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:52:10-07:00","id":935493,"title":"","content":"Yes you're right but imho werewolf's Gifts and inherent traits would still put him way ahead.<br /> On the other hand the rebalancing you mentioned would make a vampire elder serious stuff for werewolves.<br /> (And I think a very powerful Methuselah could go toe to toe even against the avatar of great fenris)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-22-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:06:33-07:00","id":935557,"title":"","content":"Actually, Revised vampires were better off because they could maintain their extra actions for more turns (one blood pool per turn instead of per level of Celerity) and got auto succussess on Potence without spending blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T13:19:25-07:00","id":935766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935491#post935491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, something that musn't be ignored with V20/DAV20:<br /> Celerity, Potence and Fortitude (when not activated with blood) passively give you extra dice to anything Dex, Strength and Stamina *on top* of any normal stats you boosted with bloodpoints.<br /> <br /> It is technically possible to make a constant-10-dex (or strength, or stamina..) non-elder Vampire straight out of chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by the time you have boosted those stats that high, you are going to be seriously need to suck up some blood!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T15:36:06-07:00","id":935839,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, blood boosting allows even neonates to perform some amazing feats, but they're going to become very hungry and prone to frenzy very quickly if they're trying to fight werewolves on an even level. It's an innate power that only really becomes super effective in the hands of low generation vampires. (Who also tend to be quite old and have impressive discipline spreads.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:59:30-07:00","id":935865,"title":"","content":"I think that V20 was not designed with the idea that vampires would fight werewolves. Otherwise, they would not have emasculated the physical disciplines like they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T19:18:17-07:00","id":935893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935865#post935865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that V20 was not designed with the idea that vampires would fight werewolves. Otherwise, they would not have emasculated the physical disciplines like they did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just V20. Vampire was never designed with the idea of fighting werewolves. VtM can have many play styles, but designing characters with the idea of fighting werewolves in mind (in physical fights) is an uphill battle. It can be done, but by default a vampire's strengths tend to be much more manipulation and subtlety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T19:59:18-07:00","id":935903,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree, it is just that they had a prayer of a chance in Revised. A beginning vampire could have Celerity 5, allowing six actions per turn, and could have sustained it for six turns in Revised before reaching half blood pool. You only get one turn in V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:46:26-07:00","id":935947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935903#post935903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I agree, it is just that they had a prayer of a chance in Revised. A beginning vampire could have Celerity 5, allowing six actions per turn, and could have sustained it for six turns in Revised before reaching half blood pool. You only get one turn in V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity is supposed to be balanced against Potence and Fortitude. It isn't, but it should be.<br /> It should not be balanced against another games mechanics (Werewolf the Apocalypse).<br /> <br /> The problem isn't that vampires can't (or stand less of a chance) fight werewolves. It's that Celerity is still much better than the other 2 physical disciplines.<br /> <br /> Also, that beginning vampire with only Celerity 5 is going to be (most likely) pretty terrible at navigating the social/political world of VtM. That is just my opinion though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T01:35:22-07:00","id":935991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935493#post935493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a very powerful Methuselah could go toe to toe even against the avatar of great fenris</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that when practically statless monster fight the outcome is totally dependent on GM fiat. <br /> <br /> In my (WtA) game you can bet your sweet pajamas that Fenris incarnate is going to win...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T01:49:31-07:00","id":935993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935766#post935766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And by the time you have boosted those stats that high, you are going to be seriously need to suck up some blood!!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying in V20 you can get a Dex 10 non-elder vamp out of chargen without spending a single blood point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T03:47:17-07:00","id":936011,"title":"","content":"You know your stuff and while i am a &quot;munchkin&quot; in computer games i really don't do that in any WoD game. Would you give me a hint where i can read up on the specification of that build?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T04:03:53-07:00","id":936017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935947#post935947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Celerity is supposed to be balanced against Potence and Fortitude. It isn't, but it should be.<br /> It should not be balanced against another games mechanics (Werewolf the Apocalypse).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed, Celerity had to be nerfed, and not because it was unbalanced against werewolves,but because it was unbalanced in fights among vampires (AKA, Celerity always won the fight).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-23-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T04:27:53-07:00","id":936020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=935991#post935991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure that when practically statless monster fight the outcome is totally dependent on GM fiat.<br /> <br /> In my (WtA) game you can bet your sweet pajamas that Fenris incarnate is going to win...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the avatar of fenris is statted in W20, just as it was statted in Get's Tribebook, and so are a lot of powerful methuselah, and stats at hand they are pretty much on even terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Avatar of Fenris has willpower 15, Rage 20,Gnosis 10, Essence 45-80<br /> Enkidu in Dragon Mythic form is gonna be STR 12, Dex 9, STA 14<br /> <br /> (Plus fire breath, 4 dice of armor and +3 dice pool at attack with bite and claws)<br /> <br /> He has brawl 9,dodge 8, Fortitude 8, Celerity 7,Potence 7<br /> <br /> <br /> This means that by V20 rules Enkidu has 28 dices to hit, 20 (str12+pot7+1 claws) dices of aggr damage, he dodges with 24 dices, 26 dices to soak lethal damage and 12 to soak aggravated damage (and, if he has combo Shatterproof he can use his stamina to soak agg, this means he coul soak up to 26 aggravated damages).<br /> <br /> Enkidu has more chances to hit (28&gt;15),more chances to dodge (24&gt;15), does the same amount of damage per turn and can soak a lot of aggravated damage .<br /> Both sides then have their personal ace card: Fenris has Blast,which with its rage dice pool can be deadly, but on other side Enkidu has a lot of extra actions he can performs, while the avatar can't.<br /> He can pull it.<br /> Sure it would be a struggle that torns open the sky and shatters the mountains, but each one of the two could win (with a bit of luck).<br /> This was just an example.<br /> <br /> Sure, on the other hand with unstatted characters it would depends on master's fiat, like...I don't know...Ur-Shulghi vs a Maeljin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-23-2016, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:53:47-07:00","id":936044,"title":"","content":"Well, it depends. A beginning vampire with Dexterity 5 and Celerity 5 attacks a beginning vampire with Stamina 5 and Fortitude 5. We will both give them knives. I think that the latter vampire will win over the former vampire because, against other supernaturals, Celerity is unimpressive without Potence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:21:28-07:00","id":936053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936011#post936011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know your stuff and while i am a &quot;munchkin&quot; in computer games i really don't do that in any WoD game. Would you give me a hint where i can read up on the specification of that build?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure!<br /> As I said before, since Celerity, Potence and Fortitude in V20/DAV20 now give dex/str/sta dice for each point in the discipline(s) when no blood points are being spent (contrary to giving str/sta autosuccesses for Potence and/or fortitude, and extra actions for celerity when blood points are spent to activate the discipline), all you need is..<br /> <br /> dex 5 + celerity 5.<br /> <br /> There you go. Permanent passive 10 dex. Likewise str 5 + potence 5, or stamina 5 + Fortitude 5. No blood spending necessary unless you want to invoke autosuccesses or extra actions instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:47:16-07:00","id":936065,"title":"","content":"V20 Fortitude does not give a passive bonus to Stamina, it only gives a passive bonus to Stamina for the purposes of soaking bashing and level damage. The difference may seem minor, but it is important for resisting certain combat maneuvers and supernatural powers. V20 Potence is a poor man's substitute for earlier form of Potence, as always having one extra die per level is much less impressive than always having one extra success per level. V20 Celerity does not even compare, I would gladly give up the passive bonus to Dexterity for only spending one blood pool per turn to gain (Celerity) extra actions rather than one blood pool per extra action (especially since you lose your passive Dexterity bonus when you take extra actions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T07:45:43-07:00","id":936082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936065#post936065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 Fortitude does not give a passive bonus to Stamina, it only gives a passive bonus to Stamina for the purposes of soaking bashing and level damage. The difference may seem minor, but it is important for resisting certain combat maneuvers and supernatural powers. V20 Potence is a poor man's substitute for earlier form of Potence, as always having one extra die per level is much less impressive than always having one extra success per level. V20 Celerity does not even compare, I would gladly give up the passive bonus to Dexterity for only spending one blood pool per turn to gain (Celerity) extra actions rather than one blood pool per extra action (especially since you lose your passive Dexterity bonus when you take extra actions).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In vampire no combat manoeuvre involves stamina:they are all dexterity or strenght related.<br /> Besides that yes, Fortitude give you a passive bonus in all physical feats in which stamina is involved.<br /> <br /> Page 258 v20<br /> <br /> &quot;Physical Feats<br /> These systems cover actions involving the three<br /> Physical Attributes (Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina).<br /> These feats typically require a roll. <b>Remember that<br /> Celerity, Fortitude, and Potence add dice to Physical<br /> Attributes</b> when making many of these rolls&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Potence still gives you extra success per level, you just have to spend a blood point.<br /> <br /> &quot;System: Each dot that the vampire has in Potence<br /> adds one die to all Strength-related dice rolls. <b>Further,<br /> the player can spend one blood point and change his<br /> Potence dice into an equal number of automatic successes</b><br /> to all Strength-related rolls for the turn. In melee<br /> and brawling combat, successes from Potence (either<br /> rolled or automatic) are applied to the damage roll<br /> results.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it still does what it did before, it's just required a blood point for the activation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then about Celerity as we said it had to be nerfed, it was really unbalanced.<br /> <br /> But consider this: in V20 extra success on attack adds to damage dice pool.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Normally, additional successes gained on a Trait roll<br /> simply mean that you do exceptionally well. I<b>n combat,<br /> each extra success you get on an attack roll equals<br /> an additional die you add automatically to your damage<br /> dice pool.</b> This creates cinematic and often fatal<br /> combat.&quot;<br /> <br /> This means that the extra dexterity Celerity gives you can come quite in handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-23-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T08:29:13-07:00","id":936094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936053#post936053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure!<br /> As I said before, since Celerity, Potence and Fortitude in V20/DAV20 now give dex/str/sta dice for each point in the discipline(s) when no blood points are being spent (contrary to giving str/sta autosuccesses for Potence and/or fortitude, and extra actions for celerity when blood points are spent to activate the discipline), all you need is..<br /> <br /> dex 5 + celerity 5.<br /> <br /> There you go. Permanent passive 10 dex. Likewise str 5 + potence 5, or stamina 5 + Fortitude 5. No blood spending necessary unless you want to invoke autosuccesses or extra actions instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you meant with celerity! I thought you meant without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T09:33:53-07:00","id":936118,"title":"","content":"Even if Fortitude is added to Stamina for physical feats, is it added to Stamina for supernatural feats or resistances? I do not see any evidence of that in V20. Anyone, Fortitude really did not change for the better, it is Potence and Celerity that changed for the worse.<br /> <br /> As for Potence, a permanent one success per level is always better than a temporary one success per level. At the very least, they could have made it competitive with the innate ability to boost Strength with blood. Even if you have V20 Potence 5, it is more cost effective to just burn blood to reach Strength 10 than to burn one blood point per turn to gain (Potence) bonus successes.<br /> <br /> I think a more equitable solution to balance the physical disciplines would have been to leave Celerity and Potence alone and to have improved Fortitude. If they had kept the Soak bonus and had added 'or you can spend one blood pool per turn to reduce the final damage of every attack against the character by (Fortitude) health levels, regardless of the source of damage. If the final damage is reduced to '0' health levels, the character also ignores any secondary effects of the attack.'. I think that version of Fortitude would have been more competitive than the current version of Fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:11:54-07:00","id":936139,"title":"","content":"The different versions of the physical Disciplines have been kind of beaten to death.<br /> <br /> Though I have no idea where you're getting your math on blood efficiency.<br /> <br /> As well, the change to Potence was made because it made grappling too good. Grapples are initiated with Strength + Brawl, and maintained with Strength + Brawl, and damage with Strength... so +X successes means it's insanely hard to dodge, insanely hard to escape, and insanely hard to not die from; unless you buy Potence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:37:32-07:00","id":936147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936118#post936118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if Fortitude is added to Stamina for physical feats, is it added to Stamina for supernatural feats or resistances? I do not see any evidence of that in V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of it, fortitude comes up also for supernatural feats and resistance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Page 172 Corrupt the undead flesh<br /> <br /> &quot;The victim\u2019s<br /> player must roll Stamina (+ Fortitude, if appropriate)<br /> against a difficulty equal to the attacker\u2019s Willpower.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dead man's hand page 186<br /> <br /> &quot;The necromancer makes the standard roll and spends<br /> two blood points for each point of Stamina (and Fortitude)<br /> possessed by the victim.&quot;<br /> <br /> Arms of the Abyss 189<br /> <br /> &quot;Each tentacle<br /> has four health levels, is affected by fire and sunlight<br /> as if it were a vampire, and soaks bashing and lethal<br /> damage using the vampire\u2019s Stamina + Fortitude.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Scorpion touch p204<br /> <br /> &quot;The victim may resist the poison with a Stamina +<br /> Fortitude roll (difficulty 6);&quot;<br /> <br /> Cobra fangs p211<br /> <br /> &quot;the venom, however, kills mortals within one minute.<br /> Bitten vampires or other supernaturally resilient creatures<br /> suffer (10 \u2013 victim\u2019s Stamina and Fortitude) levels<br /> of aggravated damage over the course of five minutes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hearth Thief p212<br /> &quot;The victim may use Fortitude to<br /> \u201csoak\u201d the attacker\u2019s successes&quot;<br /> <br /> Dehydrate page 219<br /> <br /> &quot;This power can be used on any target in the<br /> character\u2019s line of sight. The player rolls normally; the<br /> victim resists with a roll of Stamina + Fortitude (difficulty<br /> 9).&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Potence, a permanent one success per level is always better than a temporary one success per level. At the very least, they could have made it competitive with the innate ability to boost Strength with blood. Even if you have V20 Potence 5, it is more cost effective to just burn blood to reach Strength 10 than to burn one blood point per turn to gain (Potence) bonus successes. </div> </div> </div><br /> That's simply not true.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you are a 10th generation with basic STR 3 and potence 5 you need 5 blood points to get to strenght 8, besides you can spend just one blood point per turn 'cause of your generation, and even so all your buff beyond your generational maxium will drop after 3 turns.<br /> <br /> &quot;A player may spend one blood point to increase a<br /> single Physical Attribute (Strength, Dexterity, Stamina)<br /> by one dot for the duration of the scene. The player<br /> must announce at the beginning of the turn that he is<br /> doing this. A player may spend as many blood points on<br /> increasing Physical Attributes as the vampire may use<br /> in a turn (based upon Generation)<b>, but may only freely<br /> increase these Traits up to one higher than their generational maximum</b> (i.e., a Tenth-Generation vampire<br /> may increase Traits to a maximum of 6). <b>With effort, a<br /> character may increase a Physical Attribute to above<br /> this limit, but each dot above the limit lasts for only<br /> three turns </b>after the character stops spending blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it would require a huge amount of blood to reach STR 8, and it would require a lot of time.<br /> On the other hand you spend one blood point and ta da! You reached strenght 8.<br /> So we have one blood point in one turn against a serious draining done in a lot of turns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-23-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:40:35-07:00","id":936149,"title":"","content":"Then they should have based grappling off of Dexterity instead of Strength, which would have been a rather easy fix. Stronger people are not better at grappling, they are just better at dealing damage after the grapple, as anyone who has wrestled knows. A good wrestler has to have Dexterity to grapple, Strength to do damage, and Stamina to resist damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:44:09-07:00","id":936152,"title":"","content":"Dexterity to grapple? No.<br /> To hold someone you need strenght.<br /> To catch him you need dexterity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just as it is now<br /> <br /> &quot;On a successful attack roll, the attacker<br /> goes into a clinch with the target. In the first turn, the<br /> attacker may roll Strength damage. In each subsequent<br /> turn, combatants act on their orders in the initiative.<br /> A combatant can inflict Strength damage automatically<br /> or attempt to escape the clinch. No other actions<br /> are allowed until one combatant breaks free. To escape<br /> a clinch, make a resisted Strength + Brawl roll against<br /> the opponent. If the escaping character has more successes,<br /> she breaks free; if not, the characters continue<br /> to grapple in the next turn.&quot;<br /> <br /> Dexterity to catch him, Strenght to hold him.<br /> <br /> With the previous version of Potence you just had to catch him, once you had won the dexterity+brawl roll the automatic stenght success on the subsequent turns would have doomed your adversary without chance for him to escape the clinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-23-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:37:39-07:00","id":936276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936020#post936020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the avatar of fenris is statted in W20, just as it was statted in Get's Tribebook, and so are a lot of powerful methuselah, and stats at hand they are pretty much on even terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Avatar of Fenris has willpower 15, Rage 20,Gnosis 10, Essence 45-80</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, Essence was flat out 80 when it was originally statted out, and given that Nexus Crawlers and Dream Makers have enormous pools in W20 (as much as their old 2nd edition writeups had Power, as a suggested basement value), it'd be in keeping to make it more like 80+. Its specialty Charms are also as anemic as most material from pre-W20 Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Enkidu in Dragon Mythic form is gonna be STR 12, Dex 9, STA 14<br /> <br /> (Plus fire breath, 4 dice of armor and +3 dice pool at attack with bite and claws)<br /> <br /> He has brawl 9,dodge 8, Fortitude 8, Celerity 7,Potence 7<br /> <br /> <br /> This means that by V20 rules Enkidu has 28 dices to hit, 20 (str12+pot7+1 claws) dices of aggr damage, he dodges with 24 dices, 26 dices to soak lethal damage and 12 to soak aggravated damage (and, if he has combo Shatterproof he can use his stamina to soak agg, this means he coul soak up to 26 aggravated damages). </div> </div> </div>Doesn't Shatterproof cost one Willpower per use? It's not really an automatic, free-use, applies to every soak roll power, whereas the avatar can use Armor to add its Gnosis to its soak pool, for a total of 25 dice vs. everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Enkidu has more chances to hit (28&gt;15),more chances to dodge (24&gt;15), does the same amount of damage per turn and can soak a lot of aggravated damage .<br /> Both sides then have their personal ace card: Fenris has Blast,which with its rage dice pool can be deadly, but on other side Enkidu has a lot of extra actions he can performs, while the avatar can't.<br /> He can pull it.<br /> Sure it would be a struggle that torns open the sky and shatters the mountains, but each one of the two could win (with a bit of luck).<br /> This was just an example.<br /> <br /> Sure, on the other hand with unstatted characters it would depends on master's fiat, like...I don't know...Ur-Shulghi vs a Maeljin. </div> </div> </div>Spoiler: The Maeljin wins, because almost all of those Incarnae have special conditions for defeat which, unless met, result in a BAD END for the challenger. And while lots of characters would find them challenging, a lot of them have conditions that a vampire flat out wouldn't be able to arrange personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T16:15:20-07:00","id":936293,"title":"","content":"Yes, the majority of elder vampires try to ignore the existence of the spirit world's because they are not capable of dealing with the threats. That is more the Realm of the Kuei-jin than the Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T18:38:29-07:00","id":936347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936276#post936276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Spoiler: The Maeljin wins, because almost all of those Incarnae have special conditions for defeat which, unless met, result in a BAD END for the challenger. And while lots of characters would find them challenging, a lot of them have conditions that a vampire flat out wouldn't be able to arrange personally.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Truth be told Methuselahs, just as Archmages, are way more suited to destroy Maeljin than Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Let's make some examples<br /> <br /> &quot;The Archbishop of Madness, Doge Klypse<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: The only way to destroy Doge Klypse is to locate a tarnished brass box containing the name and memory of the last person he trusted before becoming a Maeljin Incarna. This box is roughly the size of a cigar box and rumored to be located somewhere in Malfeas. Opening the box sends this memory back to him, rendering him temporarily unable to be Sykora\u2019s representative. Suddenly mortal, he must perform an hour-long ritual that purges the memory, locking it in another box. Onlyduring that ritual is he vulnerable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi Auspex 8,Assamite Sorcery 9 and Obfuscation 9 here would make him way ahead any werewolf.<br /> Same goes for a Mage who mastered Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Corruption\u2019s Advocate, the Chamberlain of Lies, the Honorable Maine duBois, Esquire<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: Profiting at his expense when negotiating a contract with Maine duBois is merely a way to take his place. To destroy him, someone must find a way to cause him to sign a contract that requires him to forfeit his title if he fails to uphold his end of it. Beyond that, nobody involved in the contract may profit fromit, whether the Chamberlain of Lies succeeds in his endor not. If Maine duBois cannot fulfill the contract, heinstantly ceases to exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> For a Mithras this is a child play, with INT 9 and WIT9 he can devise a better plan than any existing werewolf.<br /> Add Subterfuge 7, Law 6, Intrigue 7,Intuition 7, no Garou in the world could make a contract loophole like him.<br /> <br /> But the same goes for any Elder wit INT 6+.<br /> <br /> Porthos too with his INT 7 and Enigmas 7 could make a nice work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Empress Aliara<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Only someone Aliara desires can destroy her. To destroy her, someone who is under her influence (see \u201cMental Taint,\u201d p. 180) must locate her, temporarily resist her charms, and while seemingly captivated by her, swear allegiance to her. As he so swears, he must steal a weapon from Aliara and use it to deliver a killing blow. The most difficult part of this act is failingto kill Aliara; he actually has sworn allegiance to her, thus giving himself over to the Wyrm. A few have tried this tactic, and Aliara enjoys collecting and playing withservants who were failed assassins.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another child play, superior dexterity + celerity to steal the dagger, willpower 10 to resist the taint, and high persuasion and charisma to cheat her.<br /> Even a strong elder like Jalan-Ajav could do this better than a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Duke of Hate, Lord Steel<br /> <br /> Destruction: Some believe that only an innocent challenging Lord Steel to battle can slay him, but innocents merely die. Others have tried fighting the Duke of Hate while filled with hatred for him, but such a victor would simply become the new Lord Steel. Instead, a would-be assassin must remove his black steel mask, weakening him by exposing the rather ordinary-looking human face beneath. Only then can his attackers capture him. They must imprison him in a well-lit chamber with mirrors in all directions, forcing him to look always at his own face \u2014 the shock of which forces him to remain within the chamber. After a full lunar month confined in this fashion, Lord Steel will rip himself apart, dying in the process. During his imprisonment, his followers will track him and attempt to free him&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even here, superior physical attribute to remove the mask, superior phyisical to imprison him.<br /> Or just be a mage with correspondece 3 and teleport his mask away and then teleport him in a mirror room.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Caliph of Pain, Lady Aife<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: Few can kill Lady Aife: the Nameless Angel of Despair, Pattern Spiders, or any similar entity that is aware of pain but is also entirely indifferent to it can kill her. The problem is of course arranging some reason for one or more of these entities to try to destroy Lady Aife.&quot;<br /> <br /> Vicissitude 6 exstatic agony, and the trick is done.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thurifuge<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: Destroying Thurifuge requires locating the purest spring of healing water in the world. It flows from the site of a powerful caern now lost to<br /> history. Splashing a few drops of water from this spring on Thurifuge will weaken him, allowing an attacker to drown the Maeljin Incarna. If Thurifuge does not drown when immersed in the spring, he will pollute the spring\u2014 forever destroying both it and the caern.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> There is no lost in history for Ur-Shulgi (8000 years old and History 9,Occult 9).<br /> Neither it would be for Kemintiri (Archeology 7, Research 6)<br /> Or for any methuselah actually.<br /> <br /> Knight Entropy<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: The only force that can destroy Lord Entropy is the pure and creative energies of the Wyld. Direct exposure to the Flux Realm would instantly kill it. Alternately, some of the Changing Breeds might discover a way to channel the power of several powerful caerns into a single site. If Knight Entropy attempts to drain this caern of power, as he has so many others, he would be overwhelmed with the Wyld\u2019s boundlesscreative energy. That force would obliterate him and his energies of decay.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy to redirect the Caern power, or if you are a mage a good use of prime and correspondence.<br /> <br /> And so on...<br /> <br /> <br /> Only with the Nameless Angel werewolves are better suited, since it requires a specific Gaian ritual.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maeljin are very tough stuff for werewolves, for vampires and mages they are far easier.<br /> <br /> So if a Werewolf can do any of this things (find the lost source, stealing Aliara's Dagger, cheat DuBois etc...) a Methuselah (or a Archmage) can do it better.<br /> <br /> It's a pure matter of stats: let's take a political animal among werewolves as Margrave Konietzko (Manipulation 5, Int 4,Wits 5, Law 3, Occult 5, Subterfuge 5) then let's take Mithras (Int 9, Wits 8, Man 9, Law 6,Subterfuge 7, Occult 5).<br /> Now, stats at hand, who's got a better chance to create a loophole in a contract? And who is more likely to persuade DuBois to sign it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For a Methuselah a Nexus Crawler or Great Fenris would be waaaaay more problematic than a Maeljin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T21:04:25-07:00","id":936403,"title":"","content":"Thaum has no power over the Umbra and Spirits are immune to Obfuscate, that's before a number of powers just don't work right in the Umbral realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T03:18:14-07:00","id":936480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936403#post936403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaum has no power over the Umbra and Spirits are immune to Obfuscate, that's before a number of powers just don't work right in the Umbral realms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That doesn't invalidate the whole point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still thaumaturgy does have power over spirits (and I don't remember anywhere it says that obfuscate doesn't work on spirits), there is a whole path (Path of the Spirit Manipulation) that is focused on dealing with spirits and level five says:<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Duality<br /> The thaumaturge<b> can now fully interact with the spiritworld</b> \u2014 a strange place that only sometimes resembles the real world. While using this power, she exists on both planes of existence at once. She is able to pick up objects in the physical world and place them in the spirit world and vice versa. Beings and landscape features in both realms are solid to her, and she can engage in any manner of interaction. <b>She can even use Thaumaturgy and other Disciplines in either world.</b> This is not without its dangers. With a single misstep, the vampire can find himself trapped in the spirit realm with no way to return home. Several incautious thaumaturges have starved into torpor while trapped on the other side of the barrier that separates the physical and spirit realms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rites of blood p144<br /> <br /> <br /> Also Necromancy shows that blood magic can work on spirits, the whole Ash Path and Sepulcher Path are involved in shadowland and ghost manipulation.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Koldunic Sorcery.<br /> <br /> And we have also Baba Yaga, in Rage across Russia we had several examples of how her Thaumaturgy could influence spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The only place in umbra where I think Thaum would not work is Flux Realm.<br /> <br /> In Axis Mundi is also stated that vampiric magic can influence spirit.<br /> <br /> page 38-39<br /> &quot;A few vampires have a magical set of Gifts which allow them to control spirits&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I really can't remember a book where it is stated that Thau or Obfu have no effect on spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:07:13-07:00","id":936712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936480#post936480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only place in umbra where I think Thaum would not work is Flux Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for where vamps just don't thread, Flux, Null Zone, lots of the Higher Umbral Courts and many of the realms of concepts and emotional constructs, the chasm, horizon realms, shard realms, sphere realms, and of course the Deep Universe. Many are just a resounding 'no', and others are definitely parts of the Umbra a Vampire does not dare to either flex any muscles or dare to thread. Not that any of those tend to be important for even exotic vampiric activities. Vampires are just not made for venturing into exotic realms of the Umbra and beyond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T15:15:45-07:00","id":936745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936712#post936712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for where vamps just don't thread, Flux, Null Zone, lots of the Higher Umbral Courts and many of the realms of concepts and emotional constructs, the chasm, horizon realms, shard realms, sphere realms, and of course the Deep Universe. Many are just a resounding 'no', and others are definitely parts of the Umbra a Vampire does not dare to either flex any muscles or dare to thread. Not that any of those tend to be important for even exotic vampiric activities. Vampires are just not made for venturing into exotic realms of the Umbra and beyond.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm sorry but is this stated somewhere?<br /> <br /> Because all a Vampire need to enter Umbra is a level 5 ritual, Umbral Walk, or Spirit Manipulation 5.<br /> <br /> Is it stated somewhere that a vampire can't get...i don't know, on the Shard Realm of Entropy for example?<br /> The only place I can think a vampire would have problem navigating is Penumbra, besides that i don't see any obstacles in exploring Near Umbra,Middle Umbra or Deep Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T15:43:28-07:00","id":936753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936480#post936480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That doesn't invalidate the whole point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Left out There is no blood magic that effects Caerns/nodes/etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still thaumaturgy does have power over spirits (and I don't remember anywhere it says that obfuscate doesn't work on spirits), there is a whole path (Path of the Spirit Manipulation) that is focused on dealing with spirits and level five says:<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Duality<br /> The thaumaturge<b> can now fully interact with the spiritworld</b> \u2014 a strange place that only sometimes resembles the real world. While using this power, she exists on both planes of existence at once. She is able to pick up objects in the physical world and place them in the spirit world and vice versa. Beings and landscape features in both realms are solid to her, and she can engage in any manner of interaction. <b>She can even use Thaumaturgy and other Disciplines in either world.</b> This is not without its dangers. With a single misstep, the vampire can find himself trapped in the spirit realm with no way to return home. Several incautious thaumaturges have starved into torpor while trapped on the other side of the barrier that separates the physical and spirit realms.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rites of blood p144 </div> </div> </div><br /> Notice how Spirit manip litterally has a power that would litterally be redundant if you could just dominate spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Necromancy shows that blood magic can work on spirits, the whole Ash Path and Sepulcher Path are involved in shadowland and ghost manipulation.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Koldunic Sorcery. </div> </div> </div>Yes there are whole effects for commanding spirits.. when generally these groups have access to dominate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And we have also Baba Yaga, in Rage across Russia we had several examples of how her Thaumaturgy could influence spirits </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga is a whole kettle of fish on her own. She had friggen Earthbound minions who knows what she could do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only place in umbra where I think Thaum would not work is Flux Realm.<br /> <br /> In Axis Mundi is also stated that vampiric magic can influence spirit.<br /> <br /> page 38-39<br /> &quot;A few vampires have a magical set of Gifts which allow them to control spirits&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I really can't remember a book where it is stated that Thau or Obfu have no effect on spirits. </div> </div> </div><br /> I will lay this out simply. How does Weather Control work in the Umbra? In the Shadowlands? Lure of Flames? The power to command spirits is NOT the power to impose ones will on Umbral realms with impunity. So &quot;Ur Shuulgi has this totally awesome ritual that would solve x&quot; doesn't work because his ritual was built to be used on Earth not Malfeas. Could he build a new one? absolutely, I mean it only took him a couple years to build one for breaking the Curse. But he would need to spend time and have access to Malfeas to well have rituals for such. <br /> <br /> and the obfuscate thing I'm trying to find but I remember a passage talking about the alien nature of spirits and mind effects not working on them as such with obfuscate included as an example. Mind you some sort of combo with SPirit manip might give what you want but I'd be hesistant to say the tools of your average nonumbrally active Methusalah are the tools for dealing with eldtrich spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T15:53:55-07:00","id":936759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936745#post936745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry but is this stated somewhere?<br /> <br /> Because all a Vampire need to enter Umbra is a level 5 ritual, Umbral Walk, or Spirit Manipulation 5.<br /> <br /> Is it stated somewhere that a vampire can't get...i don't know, on the Shard Realm of Entropy for example?<br /> The only place I can think a vampire would have problem navigating is Penumbra, besides that i don't see any obstacles in exploring Near Umbra,Middle Umbra or Deep Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spirit Manipulation 5 does not allow you to enter the Umbra. It allows you to effect the penumbra and material at the same time. <br /> <br /> Umbral walk drops you into the Penumbra. From there the would be umbra traveler has the problems of not having any real tools for going anywhere. He lacks Totems, Gifts, sphere etc to make such passages possible however nothing explicitly keeps out the un/lucky kindred from getting into Flux, Malfeas, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T16:07:08-07:00","id":936766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936759#post936759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Spirit Manipulation 5 does not allow you to enter the Umbra. It allows you to effect the penumbra and material at the same time.<br /> <br /> Umbral walk drops you into the Penumbra. From there the would be umbra traveler has the problems of not having any real tools for going anywhere. He lacks Totems, Gifts, sphere etc to make such passages possible however nothing explicitly keeps out the un/lucky kindred from getting into Flux, Malfeas, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it says it gets you in the spirit realms, last part to me seems pretty clear about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>With a single misstep, <b>the vampire can find himself trapped in the spirit realm </b>with no way to return home. Several incautious thaumaturges have starved into torpor while <b>trapped on the other side of the barrier that separates the physical and spirit realms</b>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Source for Umbral walk dropping you just in the Penumbra? Because I remember it says Umbra in general, not just Penumbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T16:13:37-07:00","id":936771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936753#post936753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Left out There is no blood magic that effects Caerns/nodes/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If sphere magick can affect nodes/Caerns, why blood magic wouldn't?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notice how Spirit manip litterally has a power that would litterally be redundant if you could just dominate spirits. </div> </div> </div>Why Redundant? Spirit Manip 3 and 4 are to dominate spirits while you are in the materiale world and you can't use discipline on them, Spirit Manip 5 let you use Disciplines in spirit worlds or using them on spirits while you are in material word, it is not redundant, they are totally different power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Baba Yaga is a whole kettle of fish on her own. She had friggen Earthbound minions who knows what she could do. </div> </div> </div>Yea, and she did those thing with Thaumaturgy 9.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will lay this out simply. How does Weather Control work in the Umbra? In the Shadowlands? Lure of Flames? </div> </div> </div><br /> The same way sphere magic would work in it?<br /> What, you think you can't cast a fireball in Umbra? Or summon a storm powering it with quintessence and prime?<br /> The only place were Force sphere would not work is Low umbra (M20 p485), besides that sphere magic works fine in most Umbra, and if sphere magic works fine I don't see why Thaum should not<br /> <br /> From the book of Madness, p121<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;As fascinating as our continuing discourse has been, it has struck me of late that we are ignoring an issue that is critical to all willworkers. As a result, I wish to address how magic, to use a blanket term, works in relation to natives of the Umbra.<br /> Quite simply, it does not always work the way a willworker might hope. <b>Superficially, each of the elements of magic appears to work as expected. </b>Correspondence effects can still connect to distance points of space. Entropic effects can still predict and degrade patterns. Life effects can still be used to<br /> heal the mage after combat. If unopposed, a willworker may never realize, however, that things can work just a bit differently in the Umbra.<br /> For one thing, outside of material realms in the Umbra,<b> matter in the spirit worlds is not the same as most mages are used to manipulating. Problems resulting from this are easily circumvented, if the mage is patient and takes the extra time to analyze any potential target material.</b> Similarly, as we have discussed before, time itself does not always behave as expected, especially at the far fringes of the Umbra. This can provide difficulties to mages used to manipulating the socalled fourth dimension. They may disbelieve their temporal perceptions or may find their intended effects expanded or contracted unexpectedly. Such annoyances, however, are only minor when one considers how the native sentients react with mystic effects.<br /> <br /> First of all, there are a significant number of Umbrood who can detect the manipulation of quintessence and who, more importantly, resent quintessence being drained away from regions they consider their personal demesne.<br /> An Umbrood potent enough to feel it merits a domain is likely to be talented enough to maintain its hold. A willworker who attempts to channel essence or fuel a pattern may find the very quintessence he is attempting to control being drained away from him, and then some. <b>More directly, a confident mage may attempt to create fireballs worthy of fiction in the relatively paradox-free Umbra.</b><br /> <b>Such effects are indeed easily channeled,</b> however, the mage may discover that Umbral opponents have ways to counteract them. More than one ill-prepared mage has been surprised as an apparently sluggish spirit displays incredible feats of speed to avoid magical effects.<br /> Fortunately, the prepared willworker has recourse when attempting to use magic against the Umbrood. <b>Mastery of spiritual magics allows the mage to directly affect the ether that makes up the beings and environment around them.</b><br /> <b>Being creatures of spirit, Umbrood have little protection against such magic except their own natural defenses.</b><br /> <b>Further, a true master of spiritual magic can shape the environment to re-create nearly any effect that can be generated in the material realms using non-spiritual masteries.</b><br /> These effects, however, cannot be easily avoided. Consider the example above, a mage forming a ball of flame from the stuff of spirit can catch even the swiftest spirit flat-footed.<br /> Using spiritual magic, manipulating reality becomes a battle of wills, and most commonly encountered spirits are no match for any willworker able to travel to the Umbra under their own power.<br /> Obviously, the examples I discuss here are just that.<br /> Other permutations are possible, and nearly any of the described difficulties can be applied to nearly any mastery of magic. I look forward to any thoughts you have.<br /> <br /> Co. Bait<br /> Lecturer Emeritus<br /> May 7th, 1998&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Seems clear to me.<br /> Spirit Manipulation is just the vampire way to recreate for Spirit Sphere, so I take they work the same way.<br /> This section seems most revaling.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Further, a true master of spiritual magic can shape the environment to re-create nearly any effect that can be generated in the material realms using non-spiritual masteries.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> So, if Sphere magic works this way in Umbra I can't see for what reason Thaumaturgy shouldn't.<br /> And, I think, that in light of this passage we can understand the definitive meaning of Spirit Manipulation level 5 in the section where it says that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>she can engage in any manner of interaction. </i><b>She can even use Thaumaturgy and other Disciplines in either world.</b> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> The power to command spirits is NOT the power to impose ones will on Umbral realms with impunity. So &quot;Ur Shuulgi has this totally awesome ritual that would solve x&quot; doesn't work because his ritual was built to be used on Earth not Malfeas. Could he build a new one? absolutely, I mean it only took him a couple years to build one for breaking the Curse. But he would need to spend time and have access to Malfeas to well have rituals for such. </div> </div> </div><br /> If we are to stand by official rules then no: Spirit Manipulation 5 makes your Thaumaturgy effective even on the spirit world, it is clearly stated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then if we want to use house rules which nullify the official rule so be it, but by official rules Thauma works in Spirit world.<br /> <br /> And again: can you find me a source which states that thaumaturgy wouldn't work in the Umbra?<br /> Because we have a lot of source who says it works and I haven't seen quoted a single one which says it doesn't<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that I'm saying It's impossible,maybe it is so, maybe I'm wrong and it is stated that Thaum doesn't work in Umbra, but i'd like to see were it is written because I don't remember reading anything like this in Infinite Tapestry,Axis Mundi and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T16:14:07-07:00","id":936772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936347#post936347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, stats at hand, who's got a better chance to create a loophole in a contract? And who is more likely to persuade DuBois to sign it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the Werewolf who can actually (possibly) get to the Maeljin. The Maeljin were set up as Werewolf big bads. That's kind of the point. The specifics of what other splats can possibly do isn't taken into account because the other game lines don't exist as such when running a Werewolf game. I'm not saying Vampires and Mages don't exist in WtA, but they certainly don't exist in the same capacity. This is how all of the game lines approach the other lines. When higher level crossovers do happen, there is a bunch of hand waving that happens and specific powers don't matter (See Ravnos and the Technocracy).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936347#post936347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a Methuselah a Nexus Crawler or Great Fenris would be waaaaay more problematic than a Maeljin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that you are picking specific Elders or powers to combat specific Maeljin. There is little chance that the specific Vampires you've chosen would come into contact with the specific Maeljin you want and from there be inclined to defeat them, and be aware of the win conditions for said Maeljin. I feel like too many deliberate story decisions would have to be put in place for any of these to be a possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936771#post936771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I'm saying It's impossible,maybe it is so, maybe I'm wrong and it is stated that Thaum doesn't work in Umbra, but i'd like to see were it is written because I don't remember reading anything like this in Infinite Tapestry,Axis Mundi and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I agree that Thaum in general would work, though specific powers might have complications or restrictions based on where they were used. None of the Umbra books are likely to mention Thaumaturgy by name though since it is specifically a Vampire power and Infinite Tapestry is a book for Mage, and Umbra and Axis Mundi are for Werewolf.<br /> You can use them as you like, but in general, the spirit worlds just weren't designed for Vampire. I'm not even sure Vampires can interact with spirits outside of powers. Like, being purely physical I think there is a decent chance that Vampires can't actually grapple/punch spirits in the Umbra, were they to physicaly go there (via the level 5 ritual). Auspex 5 sidesteps this, but has its own complications.<br /> <br /> Oh...and on the Obfuscate thing. I know Obfuscate doesn't work through the gauntlet, but if the Vampire were physically in the Umbra, I would probably rule that Obfuscate can work, but it should be countered/opposed by a Spirit's Gnosis score. Spirits are innately more aware and have perceptions that are outside of the scope of Vampire and I think that would be a good compromise. Obviously this would be a houserule, but I doubt any of the books go into vampire disciplines interacting with the spirit world, so you pretty much have to houserule that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 07-24-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T16:40:12-07:00","id":936788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936772#post936772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably the Werewolf who can actually (possibly) get to the Maeljin. The Maeljin were set up as Werewolf big bads. That's kind of the point. The specifics of what other splats can possibly do isn't taken into account because the other game lines don't exist as such when running a Werewolf game. I'm not saying Vampires and Mages don't exist in WtA, but they certainly don't exist in the same capacity. This is how all of the game lines approach the other lines. When higher level crossovers do happen, there is a bunch of hand waving that happens and specific powers don't matter (See Ravnos and the Technocracy).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a better point, obviously there is no reason for Helena walking her way to Malfeas (or Get of Fenris bidding war against Enkidu and Ur-Shulgi), it's a &quot;what if&quot;, a white room contest.<br /> Regarding Crossover I always thought that in the end White Wolf has pushed a lot to mix (badly, on balancing termis) the settings,and it seems to me that Onyxpath is pursuing the same idea of cross-setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that you are picking specific Elders or powers to combat specific Maeljin. There is little chance that the specific Vampires you've chosen would come into contact with the specific Maeljin you want and from there be inclined to defeat them, and be aware of the win conditions for said Maeljin. I feel like too many deliberate story decisions would have to be put in place for any of these to be a possibility.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Here I'm less prone to agree: as I said there is no reason for Helena tripping to Malfeas, but I still think that a Methuselah or an Archmage (without taking in account a specific Methuselah or a specific Archmage) for their inherent higher stats would have more chances than a werewolf; in the end all methuselah have similiar stats, there is not that much difference beetween Enkidu,Japeth,Helena or whoever you want, they all have very high dice pools and high discipline, sure some would be best suited than others but as a general rule I think any of them would do better than a Werewolf (just as a Werewolf would do better than a vampire in completing other task or facing other foes); and while you are right on them being less inclined to defeat them (why they should?) I think the knowledge of the win condition is something not unreachable for mystical creatures with INT 9, uncanny level of occult and mystical knowledge and thousands of years on their back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T18:10:47-07:00","id":936826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936347#post936347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Truth be told Methuselahs, just as Archmages, are way more suited to destroy Maeljin than Werewolves.<br /> <br /> Let's make some examples<br /> <br /> &quot;The Archbishop of Madness, Doge Klypse<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: The only way to destroy Doge Klypse is to locate a tarnished brass box containing the name and memory of the last person he trusted before becoming a Maeljin Incarna. This box is roughly the size of a cigar box and rumored to be located somewhere in Malfeas. Opening the box sends this memory back to him, rendering him temporarily unable to be Sykora\u2019s representative. Suddenly mortal, he must perform an hour-long ritual that purges the memory, locking it in another box. Onlyduring that ritual is he vulnerable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi Auspex 8,Assamite Sorcery 9 and Obfuscation 9 here would make him way ahead any werewolf.<br /> Same goes for a Mage who mastered Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Corruption\u2019s Advocate, the Chamberlain of Lies, the Honorable Maine duBois, Esquire<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: Profiting at his expense when negotiating a contract with Maine duBois is merely a way to take his place. To destroy him, someone must find a way to cause him to sign a contract that requires him to forfeit his title if he fails to uphold his end of it. Beyond that, nobody involved in the contract may profit fromit, whether the Chamberlain of Lies succeeds in his endor not. If Maine duBois cannot fulfill the contract, heinstantly ceases to exist.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> For a Mithras this is a child play, with INT 9 and WIT9 he can devise a better plan than any existing werewolf.<br /> Add Subterfuge 7, Law 6, Intrigue 7,Intuition 7, no Garou in the world could make a contract loophole like him.<br /> <br /> But the same goes for any Elder wit INT 6+.<br /> <br /> Porthos too with his INT 7 and Enigmas 7 could make a nice work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Empress Aliara<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Only someone Aliara desires can destroy her. To destroy her, someone who is under her influence (see \u201cMental Taint,\u201d p. 180) must locate her, temporarily resist her charms, and while seemingly captivated by her, swear allegiance to her. As he so swears, he must steal a weapon from Aliara and use it to deliver a killing blow. The most difficult part of this act is failingto kill Aliara; he actually has sworn allegiance to her, thus giving himself over to the Wyrm. A few have tried this tactic, and Aliara enjoys collecting and playing withservants who were failed assassins.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another child play, superior dexterity + celerity to steal the dagger, willpower 10 to resist the taint, and high persuasion and charisma to cheat her.<br /> Even a strong elder like Jalan-Ajav could do this better than a Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Duke of Hate, Lord Steel<br /> <br /> Destruction: Some believe that only an innocent challenging Lord Steel to battle can slay him, but innocents merely die. Others have tried fighting the Duke of Hate while filled with hatred for him, but such a victor would simply become the new Lord Steel. Instead, a would-be assassin must remove his black steel mask, weakening him by exposing the rather ordinary-looking human face beneath. Only then can his attackers capture him. They must imprison him in a well-lit chamber with mirrors in all directions, forcing him to look always at his own face \u2014 the shock of which forces him to remain within the chamber. After a full lunar month confined in this fashion, Lord Steel will rip himself apart, dying in the process. During his imprisonment, his followers will track him and attempt to free him&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even here, superior physical attribute to remove the mask, superior phyisical to imprison him.<br /> Or just be a mage with correspondece 3 and teleport his mask away and then teleport him in a mirror room.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Caliph of Pain, Lady Aife<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: Few can kill Lady Aife: the Nameless Angel of Despair, Pattern Spiders, or any similar entity that is aware of pain but is also entirely indifferent to it can kill her. The problem is of course arranging some reason for one or more of these entities to try to destroy Lady Aife.&quot;<br /> <br /> Vicissitude 6 exstatic agony, and the trick is done.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thurifuge<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: Destroying Thurifuge requires locating the purest spring of healing water in the world. It flows from the site of a powerful caern now lost to<br /> history. Splashing a few drops of water from this spring on Thurifuge will weaken him, allowing an attacker to drown the Maeljin Incarna. If Thurifuge does not drown when immersed in the spring, he will pollute the spring\u2014 forever destroying both it and the caern.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> There is no lost in history for Ur-Shulgi (8000 years old and History 9,Occult 9).<br /> Neither it would be for Kemintiri (Archeology 7, Research 6)<br /> Or for any methuselah actually.<br /> <br /> Knight Entropy<br /> <br /> &quot;Destruction: The only force that can destroy Lord Entropy is the pure and creative energies of the Wyld. Direct exposure to the Flux Realm would instantly kill it. Alternately, some of the Changing Breeds might discover a way to channel the power of several powerful caerns into a single site. If Knight Entropy attempts to drain this caern of power, as he has so many others, he would be overwhelmed with the Wyld\u2019s boundlesscreative energy. That force would obliterate him and his energies of decay.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy to redirect the Caern power, or if you are a mage a good use of prime and correspondence.<br /> <br /> And so on...<br /> <br /> <br /> Only with the Nameless Angel werewolves are better suited, since it requires a specific Gaian ritual.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maeljin are very tough stuff for werewolves, for vampires and mages they are far easier.<br /> <br /> So if a Werewolf can do any of this things (find the lost source, stealing Aliara's Dagger, cheat DuBois etc...) a Methuselah (or a Archmage) can do it better.<br /> <br /> It's a pure matter of stats: let's take a political animal among werewolves as Margrave Konietzko (Manipulation 5, Int 4,Wits 5, Law 3, Occult 5, Subterfuge 5) then let's take Mithras (Int 9, Wits 8, Man 9, Law 6,Subterfuge 7, Occult 5).<br /> Now, stats at hand, who's got a better chance to create a loophole in a contract? And who is more likely to persuade DuBois to sign it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For a Methuselah a Nexus Crawler or Great Fenris would be waaaaay more problematic than a Maeljin.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of your summations basically amount to that old saw about writing on a blackboard that unites some intricate details from an unfinished, complicated formula with the phrase &quot;...and then a miracle happens&quot;.<br /> <br /> You'd need to be more specific, except that you've just made vague assumptions. Maeljin don't have stats' opposing them is like the &quot;You Lose&quot; thing from the joke Caine sheet, except that Caine would probably lose, too; there's no defined mechanical procedure for getting one over on a being without stats, so ten dots is about as good as five, for all the good it's going to do. Additionally, there's also a standpoint to consider regarding what's written on Iris Bulb Discourse in The Thousand Hells; if the Yama Kings think that they're going to get screwed over on it due to some old Hungry Dead luminary being too well-informed about what priveleges they're owed in hell (and that's a rather specialized area of legal influence for Hungry Dead), they won't make a deal.<br /> <br /> Also, it's cute that you think that Ur-Shulgi has a long memory as a being that's only eight millennia old. The history of Werewolf actually goes back far, far further, though of course, it's not human history. Especially when you get into Mnesis, which has up to about a 230 million year range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T18:52:41-07:00","id":936841,"title":"","content":"Indeed, saying that a Methuselah would stand a better chance against a Maeljin than a Werewolf because they may have 8 extra dice on social stuff it's like saying that the average werewolf would stand a better chance than the average neonate fighting against an Antediluvian, because the werewolf it's much stronger than the neonate. Sure he is, but that doesn't mean shit to the Ante...<br /> When we get to that power level, it all depends on the Storyteller, really. It's a &quot;local&quot; cosmology issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:12:30-07:00","id":936850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936826#post936826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of your summations basically amount to that old saw about writing on a blackboard that unites some intricate details from an unfinished, complicated formula with the phrase &quot;...and then a miracle happens&quot;.<br /> <br /> You'd need to be more specific, except that you've just made vague assumptions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, they are not vaugue, they are pretty specifics.<br /> <br /> Otherwise please: show me a single Garou who could do better than Mithras against DuBois.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maeljin don't have stats' opposing them is like the &quot;You Lose&quot; thing from the joke Caine sheet </div> </div> </div>No it is not.<br /> <br /> First of all Maeljin have been killed a lot of times in the past,the only problem is that like with Voormas Second Heir curse he who kills them often becomes them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;A Maeljin Incarna serves in its position until either<br /> it fails in its duties or a more powerful avatar replaces<br /> it. If someone destroys a Dark Lord, eventually another<br /> will appear, but the world could be free of her presence<br /> for a year or even a decade. Unfortunately, <b>many of<br /> those who kill one of the Maeljin Incarna instantly<br /> replace the fallen Dark Lord,</b> leaving no more than a<br /> few minutes passing between one dying and the killer<br /> taking its place&quot;<br /> <br /> This means that they have been killed before, and it means also that every killer become the next Incarna.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [/QUOTE]except that Caine would probably lose, too[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> Nonsense, Caine will lose the day God decides Caine lose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there's no defined mechanical procedure for getting one over on a being without stats, so ten dots is about as good as five, for all the good it's going to do. </div> </div> </div>What are you saying? There is: the destruction process is very detailed, it' s pretty much clear what their destruction require and that their destruction require action that must be performed at some point, physical,social or mystical action, that can only be done through dice pool.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless if your Garou character wants to destroy the Empress he will have to steal her dagger,or will have to bargain with DuBois and so on, and that's the point:to do the required action he will have to roll dices, unless you decide he win or lose by fiat, but then also a neonate vampire could win or lose by fiat, and when the dice rolls the Methuselah has a far greater dice pool than the werewolf, and that is a fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, there's also a<br /> standpoint to consider regarding what's written on Iris Bulb Discourse in The Thousand Hells; if the Yama Kings think that they're going to get screwed over on it due to some old Hungry Dead luminary being too well-informed about what priveleges they're owed in hell (and that's a rather specialized area of legal influence for Hungry Dead), they won't make a deal. </div> </div> </div>I really don't see the problem: it's again a matter of dices and what the dices mean.<br /> Voormas had Manipulation 6 (reasoned words), Subterfuge 5 (Easy Liar), Intelligence 6, his oratory skill were beyond human, and he conviced Toh Mouh that the mating ritual would have been great, so they will not make a deal if you are the first fishmonger who was passing by, if your persuasion skill is inhuman than why they should't make the deal?<br /> So why it would be strange for Mithras with his manipulation 9 and subterfuge 7 to convince DuBois at signing a deal?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's cute that you think that Ur-Shulgi has a long memory as a being that's only eight millennia old. The history of Werewolf actually goes back far, far further, though of course, it's not human history. Especially when you get into Mnesis, which has up to about a 230 million year range. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah and I immagine that there is plenty of werewolves who have history 9 or occult 9.<br /> Do you know what history 9 means? It one step from being omniscient.<br /> With history 5 you are an authority on human history, one of the greatest historians in the world.<br /> With history 9 you are god of knowledge, there is nothing you don't know, nothing that is obscure or forgotten: has it happened? You know it.<br /> <br /> Source on the sheet of this werewolf who has better knowledge of history than Ur-Shulgi?<br /> <br /> And please, don't pull in mensis, which is only a mokole thing.Besides are you really comparing with an archmage or a methuselah with Thaum 9 or Auspex 8?<br /> <br /> With Time archsphere you can summon the past,rewind time as you like and live outside time, with Thaumaturgy 9 you can surely devise a ritual that fits the occasion, otherwise Ur-Shulgi could use his impressive high level of Auspex if needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:32:45-07:00","id":936855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936850#post936850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, they are not vaugue, they are pretty specifics.<br /> <br /> Otherwise please: show me a single Garou who could do better than Mithras against DuBois.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statless being, stats don't matter, everyone loses unless a miracle happens. Also, Mithras was a rotting flesh car for an Earthbound.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No it is not.<br /> <br /> First of all Maeljin have been killed a lot of times,the only problei is that like with Voormas Second Heir curse he who kills them often becomes them.<br /> <br /> &quot;A Maeljin Incarna serves in its position until either<br /> it fails in its duties or a more powerful avatar replaces<br /> it. If someone destroys a Dark Lord, eventually another<br /> will appear, but the world could be free of her presence<br /> for a year or even a decade. Unfortunately, <b>many of<br /> those who kill one of the Maeljin Incarna instantly<br /> replace the fallen Dark Lord,</b> leaving no more than a<br /> few minutes passing between one dying and the killer<br /> taking its place&quot;<br /> <br /> This means that they have been killed before, and it means also that not all the killers become the next Incarna. </div> </div> </div>And none of them have been Vampire characters!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nonsense, Caine will lose the day God decides Caine lose. </div> </div> </div>Not a part of Werewolf, don't care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are you saying? There is: the destruction process is very detailed, it' s pretty much clear what their destruction require and that their destruction require action that must be performed at some point, physical,social or mystical action, that can only be done through dice pool. </div> </div> </div>No, it never says that rolling is involved. Again, statless being, rolls need not apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nevertheless if your Garou character wants to destroy the Empress he will have to steal her dagger,or will have to bargain with DuBois and so on, and that's the point:to do the required action he will have to roll dices, unless you decide he win or lose by fiat, but then also a neonate vampire could win or lose by fiat, and when the dice rolls the Methuselah has a far greater dice pool than the werewolf, and that is a fact. </div> </div> </div>Newwwwwwp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't see the problem: it's again a matter of dices and what the dices mean.<br /> Voormas had Manipulation 6 (reasoned words), Subterfuge 5 (Easy Liar), Intelligence 6, his oratory skill were beyond human, and he conviced Toh Mouh that the mating ritual would have been great, so they will not make a deal if you are the first fishmonger who was passing by, if your persuasion skill is inhuman than why they should't make the deal?<br /> So why it would be strange for Mithras with his manipulation 9 and subterfuge 7 to convince DuBois at signing a deal? </div> </div> </div>Because Maine is expecting it. And also doesn't need to roll to resist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah and I immagine that there is plenty of werewolves who have history 9 or occult 9.<br /> Do you know what history 9 means? It one step from being omniscient.<br /> With history 5 you are an authority on human history, one of the greatest historians in the world.<br /> With history 9 you are god of knowledge, there is nothing you don't know, nothing that is obscure or forgotten: has it happened? You know it. </div> </div> </div>No, you don't. You have a meaningless inflated number that involves chucking more dice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Source on the sheet of this werewolf who has better knowledge of history than Ur-Shulgi? </div> </div> </div>Mnesis 5 means that you have access to all the memories of your ancestors, as a Mokole specialty, and it goes back to the Early Triassic, back before mammals existed. Even Garou and other Fera can consult their Ancestors, which have been around for quite some time, given the timeline set out in Shattered Dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:34:39-07:00","id":936856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936841#post936841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, saying that a Methuselah would stand a better chance against a Maeljin than a Werewolf because they may have 8 extra dice on social stuff it's like saying that the average werewolf would stand a better chance than the average neonate fighting against an Antediluvian, because the werewolf it's much stronger than the neonate. Sure he is, but that doesn't mean shit to the Ante...<br /> When we get to that power level, it all depends on the Storyteller, really. It's a &quot;local&quot; cosmology issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it all fall son the fiat of the master than also a neonate could destroy the Maeljin, or a Rank1 could kill Tzimisce, of course.<br /> <br /> game mechanics at hands you will have to perform those actions, and dice pool will determine the outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:49:52-07:00","id":936863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936855#post936855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Statless being, stats don't matter, everyone loses unless a miracle happens. Also, Mithras was a rotting flesh car for an Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stats matter as long you have to perform actions.<br /> When your werewolf will have to steal the dagger of the empress what will happen? You will make him roll the dice or you will go by fiat?<br /> Because by fiat also a very luck neonate vampire can steal the dagger, and that would mean that the whole argument is pointless: Maeljin can be killed by anyone as long as the master wish, but then we have a nice lore and consistency problem, don't you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And none of them have been Vampire characters! </div> </div> </div>Any source or is just an assumption?<br /> <br /> It is not told who killed the previous Maeljin, it could have been a fae,a mummy, a mage, anyone might have been for what are we told and for what we know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not a part of Werewolf, don't care. </div> </div> </div>And who cares of what do you care? It's the same setting, the same world, even in werewolf and mage world Caine does exist (as it is stated in many books, even the last book of the wyrm says that the vampiric curse is derived from Caine.<br /> <br /> Book of the wyrm p141<br /> <br /> &quot;Vampires are hard to possess. Perhaps the Curse of<br /> Caine is such a potent form of damnation that any lesser<br /> affliction has trouble taking root; perhaps it has something<br /> to do with vampires already being dead.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah it is werewolf world, then if you decide to ignore it because you use your own setting of house rules it's another matter.<br /> Despite this yeah, Caine exist also in Werewolf world, just as he exist in Mage world, just as the Wyrm exist in Mage, and the Consensus exist in Vampire, you can tap your ears and close your eyes, but is a fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it never says that rolling is involved. Again, statless being, rolls need not apply. </div> </div> </div>So you are confirming that a vampire neonate could totally pull it right? No roll involved, it's just master's will.<br /> <br /> The book saysthat actions are involved, which, you may have forgot, in RPG are done through dice rolling<br /> <br /> Remember page 232 of W20? <br /> <br /> Attempting an action is simple enough. Tell the Storyteller<br /> what you want your character to do, and how she\u2019s<br /> going to do it. Most things that your character attempts<br /> are simple enough to be automatically successful. <b>When<br /> the Storyteller has reasonable doubt as to whether you\u2019ll<br /> succeed or fail, and has interesting possibilities lined up for<br /> both, you will have to roll dice to determine the results</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember? RPG 101?<br /> <br /> Or, again, will your player kill the Maeljin by fiat?<br /> <br /> <br /> It is simple: either your player will do this by fiat or will he roll the dices to perform the action, tertium non datur.<br /> <br /> If it is done by fiat then the whole argument has no meaning: of course a Methuselah could pull it, even a child could pull it if the master think that it would fit the story; so if it does fit that Menele (or Patrick the neonate vampire) kills DuBois then so be it, they will.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it is done by rolling then he who has the higher dice pool will have better chances to perform the action.<br /> <br /> Tertium non datur, pick your choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, you don't. You have a meaningless inflated number that involves chucking more dice. </div> </div> </div>No I'm sorry, those dice pools means something, something that is explained in each manual at the page of skill and attribute, sorry you didn't get it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Look, since for you just Werewolf is relevant I will quote the W20<br /> <br /> Page 123<br /> <br /> &quot;Attributes<br /> <b>All characters in Werewolf: The Apocalypse have<br /> Attributes, representing the basic abilities of human<br /> beings and similar creatures. The majority of people have<br /> Attributes rated between 1 dot (poor) and 3 dots (good).<br /> A few gifted individuals \u2014 including the pack \u2014 can have<br /> ratings of 4 (excellent) or 5 (world-class).</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Again, page 132<br /> <br /> &quot;The Academics Knowledge represents the character\u2019s<br /> education in the humanities: literature, history, art, philosophy,<br /> linguistics, and other subjects normally encompassed under the<br /> banner of \u201cliberal arts.\u201d A high Academics rating indicates a<br /> well-rounded knowledge in many of these fields, along with<br /> expertise in one in particular. A player must always choose<br /> a specialty in Academics, even when her character has less<br /> than four dots in the Skill.<br /> \u2022 Student: You know Henry VIII sure liked the<br /> ladies.<br /> \u2022\u2022 College: You can quote from the classics of literature,<br /> identify major cultural movements, and<br /> understand the shift of languages over time.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Masters: You could get a paper published on your<br /> area of expertise.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Doctorate: When they say you wrote the book<br /> on the subject, it isn\u2019t a metaphor.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Scholar: In your field, you are one of the ultimate<br /> voices of authority.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if with accademic 5 you are one of the ultimate voices of authority,what are you with accademic 9?<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's see what traits over 5 means.<br /> <br /> These are examples of attributes over 5, from Mummy the Resurrection,since these attributes are mystical endowment they will not be exactly the same for vampire, but they are a good starting point to understand what a trait above 5 means..<br /> <br /> <br /> Manipulation<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> 6 Absorbing. You can place a single individual in a mild hypnotic trance with a succesful resisted Manipulation versus Willpower roll. Lasting the scene, you can direct the subject to perform minor trask as long as the do no threaten her<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 7 Enthralling. With a successful resisted Manipulation versus Willpower roll,you can impant a post-hypnotic suggestion for a target to perform later, as long as it doesn't threaten her life.<br /> <br /> 8 Enslaving. As under 6, but your influence continues even when you're not around, so that teh subject feels inclined to look out for your best interest as long as doing so doesn't put her in danger. </div> </div> </div><br /> Intelligence<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> 6 Eidetic Memory. You have an encyclopedic pool fo knowledge. You can decipher puzzles or mysteries with minimal clues.<br /> <br /> 7 Intuitive understanding. You may make Intelligence rolls regarding matters in which you don't have actual Skill or Knowledges.<br /> <br /> 8 Universal mind. Your mind is in tune with the cosmic consciousness. Spending at least an hour contemplating the divine order grants one level per success on an intelligence roll for any knowledge skill or talen. This temporary rating last for one scene </div> </div> </div>And Mithras has Int 9 and Manip 9.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mnesis 5 means that you have access to all the memories of your ancestors, as a Mokole specialty, and it goes back to the Early Triassic, back before mammals existed. Even Garou and other Fera can consult their Ancestors, which have been around for quite some time, given the timeline set out in Shattered Dreams. </div> </div> </div>You just have to create a Thaumaturgy 9 ritual to unfold the events of the past, using a time archspere or Auspex 9 Sight of the Oracle and you will have the same result, it's just required blood and time, or time and quintessence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, it is not even necessary: the previous stats should explain pretty well everything. Ur-Shulgi, with his Int 9 history 9 just has to close his burned eyes,atune himself for some minutes with the divine order of the universe and he will have all the answers he was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 07-24-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:01:21-07:00","id":936869,"title":"","content":"Actually, we do not know if Caine even exists in Vampire or if he is just a product of the insanity of the Antediluvians. We know that there are scenarios that occur if Caine does exist, but the Caine myth itself did not exist in Jewish tradition until after the Babylonian exile, so I doubt that Caine is anything more than a progenitor borrowed from Christianity during the 5th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:47:41-07:00","id":936904,"title":"","content":"In the canon novels Cain does exist, he is even one of the characters (Kapaneous).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T21:42:07-07:00","id":936919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936863#post936863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see what traits over 5 means.<br /> <br /> These are examples of attributes over 5, from Mummy the Resurrection,since these attributes are mystical endowment they will not be exactly the same for vampire, but they are a good starting point to understand what a trait above 5 means..<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Try not to quote from Mummy. Their powers specifically give magical abilities if they push your stats above 5. A vampire that blood buff to Str 8 doesn't do Agg with their fists. A GArou with Stamina 8 doesnt get 3 extra health levels and take half damage from lethal. Those are specifically a thing for when you are playing Mummy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936863#post936863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, it is not even necessary: the previous stats should explain pretty well everything. Ur-Shulgi, with his Int 9 history 9 just has to close his burned eyes,atune himself for some minutes with the divine order of the universe and he will have all the answers he was looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if the Dif is 9 or 10 (quite possible) it just means he has a better chance of botching.<br /> Please realize that these are creatures from WtA. You may choose to run a fully integrated World of Darkness with absolutely every creature ever mentioned running around. This is not necessarily the default. Not once in a Vampire book have they mentioned Thunderwyrms (to my knowledge). For the sake of Vampire, they don't seem to exist. You would think something like that would have come up at some point if they did.<br /> It can be fun to pull obscure stuff from different game lines to give players an unexpected surprise, but the other game lines are their own games. The assumptions about an individual game's universe does not necessarily carry over into another game line.<br /> <br /> For me, the reason Vampires can't usurp the Maeljin is because unless you are specifically playing a crossover game, Ur-Shulgi and Maeljin don't exist in the same universe. If you are playing a crossover game, then the ST needs to decide what is and isn't true and can then make up reasons for stuff like this.<br /> Personally, most vampires have no knowledge of the Umbra, and certainly less knowledge of Umbral realms, and then even less knowledge of the creatures buried deep within them.....and then know even less than that about their unique weaknesses. Have your 18 dice pool roll at dif 10 and see how that goes for you. From there, the Vampire can work on actually accomplishing the task, assuming they can get to the Umbra, avoid the spirits, find a path to Malfeas, avoid spirit armies, and find a way to the specific Maeljin they are looking for. Seems easy enough. What would be more amusing would be if after all of that, some other Vampire had already accomplished this, so the new Vampire can face off against some other (no un-Maeljin'ed) Methuselah. Seems like a funny idea to me actually.<br /> Bue again, that assumes you want to run all the Universes together and you decide that's how things work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936904#post936904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the canon novels Cain does exist, he is even one of the characters (Kapaneous).</div> </div> </div> </div>Novel canon and in game canon are 2 very separate creatures.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 07-25-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T22:36:02-07:00","id":936936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936766#post936766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, it says it gets you in the spirit realms, last part to me seems pretty clear about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>With a single misstep, <b>the vampire can find himself trapped in the spirit realm </b>with no way to return home. Several incautious thaumaturges have starved into torpor while <b>trapped on the other side of the barrier that separates the physical and spirit realms</b>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Source for Umbral walk dropping you just in the Penumbra? Because I remember it says Umbra in general, not just Penumbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Penumbra is where you enter everything from? The description of the Spirit world for SPirit manip matches the Penumbra... I'm pretty sure if the effect was enter a realm it would discuss such.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936771#post936771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If sphere magick can affect nodes/Caerns, why blood magic wouldn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Create a mind with Thaum. Or a Wonder. or Travel to an alternative Universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why Redundant? Spirit Manip 3 and 4 are to dominate spirits while you are in the materiale world and you can't use discipline on them, Spirit Manip 5 let you use Disciplines in spirit worlds or using them on spirits while you are in material word, it is not redundant, they are totally different power. </div> </div> </div><br /> Does auspex not work across then when you use hermetic sight or does it require Spirit manip 5 to use heightened senses on the umbra?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yea, and she did those thing with Thaumaturgy 9. </div> </div> </div>And pure Fiat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same way sphere magic would work in it?<br /> What, you think you can't cast a fireball in Umbra? Or summon a storm powering it with quintessence and prime?<br /> The only place were Force sphere would not work is Low umbra (M20 p485), besides that sphere magic works fine in most Umbra, and if sphere magic works fine I don't see why Thaum should not<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> From the book of Madness, p121<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;As fascinating as our continuing discourse has been, it has struck me of late that we are ignoring an issue that is critical to all willworkers. As a result, I wish to address how magic, to use a blanket term, works in relation to natives of the Umbra.<br /> Quite simply, it does not always work the way a willworker might hope. <b>Superficially, each of the elements of magic appears to work as expected. </b>Correspondence effects can still connect to distance points of space. Entropic effects can still predict and degrade patterns. Life effects can still be used to<br /> heal the mage after combat. If unopposed, a willworker may never realize, however, that things can work just a bit differently in the Umbra.<br /> For one thing, outside of material realms in the Umbra,<b> matter in the spirit worlds is not the same as most mages are used to manipulating. Problems resulting from this are easily circumvented, if the mage is patient and takes the extra time to analyze any potential target material.</b> Similarly, as we have discussed before, time itself does not always behave as expected, especially at the far fringes of the Umbra. This can provide difficulties to mages used to manipulating the socalled fourth dimension. They may disbelieve their temporal perceptions or may find their intended effects expanded or contracted unexpectedly. Such annoyances, however, are only minor when one considers how the native sentients react with mystic effects.<br /> <br /> First of all, there are a significant number of Umbrood who can detect the manipulation of quintessence and who, more importantly, resent quintessence being drained away from regions they consider their personal demesne.<br /> An Umbrood potent enough to feel it merits a domain is likely to be talented enough to maintain its hold. A willworker who attempts to channel essence or fuel a pattern may find the very quintessence he is attempting to control being drained away from him, and then some. <b>More directly, a confident mage may attempt to create fireballs worthy of fiction in the relatively paradox-free Umbra.</b><br /> <b>Such effects are indeed easily channeled,</b> however, the mage may discover that Umbral opponents have ways to counteract them. More than one ill-prepared mage has been surprised as an apparently sluggish spirit displays incredible feats of speed to avoid magical effects.<br /> Fortunately, the prepared willworker has recourse when attempting to use magic against the Umbrood. <b>Mastery of spiritual magics allows the mage to directly affect the ether that makes up the beings and environment around them.</b><br /> <b>Being creatures of spirit, Umbrood have little protection against such magic except their own natural defenses.</b><br /> <b>Further, a true master of spiritual magic can shape the environment to re-create nearly any effect that can be generated in the material realms using non-spiritual masteries.</b><br /> These effects, however, cannot be easily avoided. Consider the example above, a mage forming a ball of flame from the stuff of spirit can catch even the swiftest spirit flat-footed.<br /> Using spiritual magic, manipulating reality becomes a battle of wills, and most commonly encountered spirits are no match for any willworker able to travel to the Umbra under their own power.<br /> Obviously, the examples I discuss here are just that.<br /> Other permutations are possible, and nearly any of the described difficulties can be applied to nearly any mastery of magic. I look forward to any thoughts you have.<br /> <br /> Co. Bait<br /> Lecturer Emeritus<br /> May 7th, 1998&quot;<br /> </div> </div> </div>From mage 20<br /> <br /> Realms: Each Realm is a reality unto itself. The physics of<br /> one Realm might differ considerably from the principles of other<br /> Realms, each Realm following the essence of its specific place. A<br /> Chinese Hell, an animistic Nature Realm, the Machine-Haven<br /> Autocthonia, and the Umbral Realm of Forces all run by very<br /> different rules, and none of them bears much resemblance to<br /> Earth\u2019s reality<br /> <br /> <br /> This is under a section of reality zones and how True magick has diffrent levels of difficulty depending on area, and how vulgar it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems clear to me.<br /> Spirit Manipulation is just the vampire way to recreate for Spirit Sphere, so I take they work the same way.<br /> This section seems most revaling.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Further, a true master of spiritual magic can shape the environment to re-create nearly any effect that can be generated in the material realms using non-spiritual masteries.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> So, if Sphere magic works this way in Umbra I can't see for what reason Thaumaturgy shouldn't.<br /> And, I think, that in light of this passage we can understand the definitive meaning of Spirit Manipulation level 5 in the section where it says that. </div> </div> </div>Mage 20 again!<br /> <br /> Static magic conforms to rigid constraints. The Obfuscation Discipline, for example, has a range of effects that hide<br /> or disguise the vampire; all of them, however, have specific things they can do within a small variety of level-based<br /> powers. The same\u2019s true for Garou Gifts, changeling cantrips, and so on. A variety of magic-using humans can use such<br /> powers too: hunters, psychics, hedge magicians, etc. In all cases, though, their powers operate within tight parameters<br /> of what is and is not possible with them. As magical as they are, their effects \u2013 both within the story world and within<br /> the game\u2019s rules \u2013 are static. Whether it\u2019s because Kindred and Garou have awakened their spirits to a predetermined<br /> path, because centuries of folklore have integrated their powers into reality, or maybe elements of both explanations,<br /> the effects and limitations remain constant and Paradox-free.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So no Spirit manip is not the equal to Spirit sphere. It doesn't let you change the gauntlet. It doesn't let you send others into the Umbra. It doesn't let you break the Dreamshell.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we are to stand by official rules then no: Spirit Manipulation 5 makes your Thaumaturgy effective even on the spirit world, it is clearly stated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then if we want to use house rules which nullify the official rule so be it, but by official rules Thauma works in Spirit world.<br /> <br /> And again: can you find me a source which states that thaumaturgy wouldn't work in the Umbra?<br /> Because we have a lot of source who says it works and I haven't seen quoted a single one which says it doesn't<br /> <br /> <br /> Not that I'm saying It's impossible,maybe it is so, maybe I'm wrong and it is stated that Thaum doesn't work in Umbra, but i'd like to see were it is written because I don't remember reading anything like this in Infinite Tapestry,Axis Mundi and so on. </div> </div> </div><br /> No, Spirit manip 5 lets you act in both the material and Penumbra at teh same time. It can by messing up enter the Umbra.. it can't leave. The laws of the Penumbra are more ore less the same as the physical.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say &quot;I can use lure of Flame in the Elemental realm of water!&quot; A true mage who'd try fireball in said area would get paradox and have a harder time using it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T01:34:43-07:00","id":936981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936745#post936745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but is this stated somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't mentioned in any Vampire books. Because almost none of those realms are even mentioned in any Vampire material in the first place.<br /> <br /> But, for the sake of crossoverness, let's give it a go.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let me point out something important about Spirit Manipulation 5:<br /> <br /> First off, it makes you exist in a dual state (Hence the name 'Duality' for that level of Spirit Manip), being in the real world and 'Spirit Realm' at once. There is only one described layer that even mirrors the real world, and that's the <i>Penumbra</i>. Anything deeper and there would be no 'Duality' anymore, and outside the scope of Spirit Manip 5.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System: The thaumaturge may interact with the spirit world for <b>fifteen minutes</b>. Each additional level of success on the activation roll increases the duration of this power by an <b>additional fifteen minutes</b>. Duality can only be enacted while the character begins the process in the physical world. </div> </div> </div>Even if you *<i>could</i>* go deeper with this ability, you wouldn't travel far, especially not to any exotic realms, because of the time constraints.<br /> If you accidentally somehow were to trap yourself in the Penumbra (like with a botch), good luck returning. You can't activate Duality from the spirit worlds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only place I can think a vampire would have problem navigating is Penumbra </div> </div> </div>What? That's the easiest place to navigate and get into. It mirrors the real world layout for the most part. It's <i>exactly</i> the part that Spirit Manip 5 allows you to see and interact with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, &quot;Umbral Walk&quot; is much more of a fitting ability here, however it only gets the Vampire sidestepping into the Middle Umbra (As described as 'The Land Of Eternal Night' in the Umbral Walk text).<br /> From there on it's all exploration by foot, hoping you can actually manage to hold conversations with the spirits there, understand the exotic landscape and sights in the first place, not get lost (As the Vampire is pretty much naked on sidestepping and has to keep everything in their head), and last but not least, get back before you're out of blood. And don't get mauled by Werewolves.<br /> <br /> And that's just the normal Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> I didn't say that a Vampire *<i>can't</i>* get to any more exotic realms. But it's highly hazardous, with no easy blood sources, no equipment, unfamiliar sights, nasty enemies and only being able to write down all that you have learned on successful return. *<i>if</i>* you are able to go there in the first place, which requires a level 5 RItual.<br /> <br /> So, on top of a very limited amount of Vampires even being able to go there, you have an even smaller number that manages to go too far, even fewer that probably would return from such a far trip and write their knowledge down, and even fewer that will probably share that knowledge.<br /> <br /> \u200bAll in all there's a reason why most of those realms don't even get mention in the books, unlike with the Mage and Werewolf gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-25-2016, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:28:54-07:00","id":937216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=936904#post936904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the canon novels Cain does exist, he is even one of the characters (Kapaneous).</div> </div> </div> </div>We have someone who claims to be Caine, who thinks he is Caine, but he cannot be Caine because the myth of Caine did not exist until around 500 BCE. The Gehenna novels represent a possible scenario for the vampire race that requires the existence of Caine, but that does not mean that Caine is required to exist for vampires to exist. I believe that it makes more sense, given the archeological evidence, that Caine is a delusion created by the Antediluvians when they became the founders. If he exists, he is a spirit of madness created from a gestalt of the insanity of the Antediluvians, and 'he' is born from the power of the Antediluvians rather than the Antediluvians being descended from him.<br /> <br /> The Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand discusses vampire travel to the Low Umbra (and why the Black Hand kills anyone who attempts to go to the Deep Umbra). The Kuei-jin are capable of traveling to the Middle Umbra and the Low Umbra, though they are much more capable of that sort of thing than the Kindred. It would be interesting if there was a bloodline that could access the Middle Umbra though, perhaps the survivors of the Telyavelic Tremere could have escaped into the Middle Umbra after developing a Discipline (or Path) that could allow them to feed on spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:58:46-07:00","id":937268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=937216#post937216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have someone who claims to be Caine, who thinks he is Caine, but he cannot be Caine because the myth of Caine did not exist until around 500 BCE. The Gehenna novels represent a possible scenario for the vampire race that requires the existence of Caine, but that does not mean that Caine is required to exist for vampires to exist. I believe that it makes more sense, given the archeological evidence, that Caine is a delusion created by the Antediluvians when they became the founders. If he exists, he is a spirit of madness created from a gestalt of the insanity of the Antediluvians, and 'he' is born from the power of the Antediluvians rather than the Antediluvians being descended from him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what makes the most sense? Not having undead hemophages that wander around and go on gritty adventures; that really does sync best with all available scientific evidence.<br /> <br /> Ye gods, you can have mythological figures in a game about mythological creatures.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:13:33-07:00","id":937279,"title":"","content":"Yes, but Caine does not have to exist for vampires to exist, and Caine is a really minor mythological figure from a legend that is only 2500 years old (the legend of Set predates the legend of Caine by a minimum of 2500 years). Caine is nothing more than a mythological representation of the fear that ancient pastoralists felt over the numerically superior ancient horticulturalists, which is why Caine (the farmer) was the first murderer and why Abel (the herder) was the first victim of murder. Caine's involvement with vampires is just a fictional invention of WW and is found in none of the legends or myths of vampires.<br /> <br /> In fact, even the majority of the members of the vampire race in the WoD (the vampires of Africa and India) seem to think that Caine is nothing more than a form of cultural imperialism by vampires who belonged to Abrahamic religions when they were mortal (or who adopted Abrahamic religions after their Embrace). Heck, it would make more sense, from a mythological point of view, if Set was the first vampire, at least the founder of the vampires would have been a god of darkness rather than an incompetent murderer. Which would be amusing because it would mean that the Followers of Set are actually correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:24:36-07:00","id":937328,"title":"","content":"And the Dark Ages book about the Norse vampires of ye olde (Wolves by the Sea? Something like that) features their own creation myth, where Odin gave a dieing warrior eternal life with his blood, and he became the first vampire. Then the Norse vampires actually were living with the normal humans in their villages as praised warriors of Odin, taking care of each other, and the Vampires going along the raids and traderoutes of the viking ships.<br /> <br /> It's really neat stuff. So yeah, lots of fancy Vampire origin stories. Take your pick.<br /> <br /> As for Caine,<br /> If he were the de-facto real origin, just because his current myth itself is 2500 years old doesn't mean that it isn't much older and the story simply got changed and adjusted over time. Nor does it mean he couldn't have been the 8 - 9000 years old that he supposedly is. It's not like news spread via newspapers during those days, humans were much fewer, and neither can I imagine him running around the first hundred or thousand years shouting 'Look, I'm Caine!'. Myths build up over time, they change, and morph and adjust to the political and social changes of the world.<br /> <br /> Hence sudden Christian myth around, well, that time. Perhaps the older tales about him are simply long forgotten and replaced, just like Christianity's holidays basically were made by taking pagan rites and dates and replacing them with their own versions.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, from a sober perspective...it's the WoD. Come on, folks;<br /> All the books are written from a certain IC perspective of a specific faction.<br /> <br /> Caine might be the real deal. He might not. Maybe the other creation myths are right.<br /> And let's not get started on the huge incompatibilities of Origin stories of the World of Darkness between the gamelines themselves. There's a reason Demon had to resort to 'It was kind of everything at once because it was all just representations on a different dimensional point of view' to even remotely make it all work, and yet it still immediately was biased on THEIR perspective.<br /> <br /> If an ST wants to make Caine the true origin, go for it. The Gehenna Campain endgame book (Not the novels) has Caine pop up in one of the possible scenarios, along with Lilith, and them going toe to toe. In other scenarios, he doesn't play a role. Yet other gameline scenarios have a completely different take.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't try to put too much reason and historical logic behind things. Enjoy the ride. Use what fits your game.<br /> Anything else will make people argue about things that don't fit together in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-25-2016, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:52:06-07:00","id":937346,"title":"","content":"Thank you. Every ST has to decide which origin myth fits their campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T18:14:42-07:00","id":941567,"title":"","content":"Demons can get fairly nasty with melee stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T02:19:09-07:00","id":941776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=941567#post941567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can get fairly nasty with melee stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Most major splats can, but I still say that the one very thing that would make my character (*almost* independent of what the character is, unless the character is something like an Archmage..), hold still, nod and smile, is a high ranking Wyrsta Ananasi. If my character knew what they are facing.<br /> <br /> It's like that wasp meme.<br /> Hold still, chill out, and hope the Wyrsta decides not to put you on its list of stuff to fsck up that day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-02-2016, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:03:21-07:00","id":941879,"title":"","content":"What about a beginning Wyrsta Ananasi? The problem that they have is they lack Rage and Regeneration. While they have aggravated soak and their shape shifting abilities, I am not sure if they are better than vampires. I do know that they are probably beaten by every Changing Breed though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:22:16-07:00","id":941891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=941879#post941879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a beginning Wyrsta Ananasi? The problem that they have is they lack Rage and Regeneration. While they have aggravated soak and their shape shifting abilities, I am not sure if they are better than vampires. I do know that they are probably beaten by every Changing Breed though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the beginning? Oh, no. Nothing special at all, really. And definitely nowhere near the higher ranks of out-of-cgen fighters at all. They can only spend one blood at that point per round, too.<br /> Starting with Rank 3, things get crazy though. At Rank 4 even more so.<br /> <br /> Just to explain the dark, scary core of this nightmare fuel combination of changing breed and Ananasi faction:<br /> ...would you give lip to a creature that can get a +8-9 strength bonus(!) with Pithus form + a gift (Hydraulic Strength), and 15 attacks in one round due to an increased blood pool (Tick Body) and another gift fueling both those things to their max in the same first round (Blood Pump. No, there is no stated limit on blood spending or number of extra attacks with that one.)?<br /> <br /> Yeah. They'd be completely drained after that, but you're quite simply not standing anymore. Barely anything is. If they managed to save up some blood due to not going all-out, they can heal 6 damage in the next round, unless it's aggravated. Which silver won't do in their case. Then they suck your corpse dry to fuel up again.<br /> <br /> The only redeeming factor is that Ananasi are not angry, nor are Wyrstas much along the lines of open aggressors. Just stay out of their crosshairs unless they're young.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-02-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T09:07:34-07:00","id":944357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/932215-is-it-accurate-to-claim-that-werewolves-are-the-best-melee-fighters-in-cwod?p=941891#post941891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At the beginning? Oh, no. Nothing special at all, really. And definitely nowhere near the higher ranks of out-of-cgen fighters at all. They can only spend one blood at that point per round, too.<br /> Starting with Rank 3, things get crazy though. At Rank 4 even more so.<br /> <br /> Just to explain the dark, scary core of this nightmare fuel combination of changing breed and Ananasi faction:<br /> ...would you give lip to a creature that can get a +8-9 strength bonus(!) with Pithus form + a gift (Hydraulic Strength), and 15 attacks in one round due to an increased blood pool (Tick Body) and another gift fueling both those things to their max in the same first round (Blood Pump. No, there is no stated limit on blood spending or number of extra attacks with that one.)?<br /> <br /> Yeah. They'd be completely drained after that, but you're quite simply not standing anymore. Barely anything is. If they managed to save up some blood due to not going all-out, they can heal 6 damage in the next round, unless it's aggravated. Which silver won't do in their case. Then they suck your corpse dry to fuel up again.<br /> <br /> The only redeeming factor is that Ananasi are not angry, nor are Wyrstas much along the lines of open aggressors. Just stay out of their crosshairs unless they're young.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Taking more actions through rage (and we'd assume blood too) than you have in dex/wits imposes a significant penalty to every action you take. This significantly cripples the spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:48:45-07:00","id":944409,"title":"","content":"Yes, a +3 difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T11:00:40-07:00","id":944417,"title":"","content":"In light of the sheer amount of extra actions, and the high damage roll resulting from only a single success hit... I am not sure. It makes too much of a difference in the end result. <br /> <br /> Although that reminds me to actually calculate the average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:21:48-07:00","id":944494,"title":"","content":"A base difficulty of 9 isn't great, because a single botch is generally suggested to result in a situation that ends the rest of the spam of attacks. At difficulty 9, the odds are very much against you finishing 15 attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:34:35-07:00","id":944503,"title":"","content":"Biting is dif 5 still isn't it (as of W20)? That would <i>only</i> dif 8 which shouldn't be too bad. Along with the Dex bonus of an alternate form, they should reliably be able to hit with most/all bite attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T14:05:17-07:00","id":944510,"title":"","content":"I feel like anything ridiculously excessive warrants more than +3 difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:48:38-07:00","id":944576,"title":"","content":"Honestly, anything that is &quot;ridiculously excessive&quot; should just be disallowed instead of raising the difficulty to make it mechanically impossible.<br /> If you (as ST) find flaw or exploit in the system, just fix it instead of penalizing the players for finding it. Just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T16:23:23-07:00","id":944589,"title":"","content":"Oh, definitely. ST regulating starts way below this, but by RAW, I consider this pretty much the answer to the melee showdown <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That said, I'd keep the 'above wits gets +3' rule, and add an 'above dex is impossible' houserule. It evens the odds for all concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thanked